msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:660 ac796ae064c04258b63d7dac4189ff00
msgid ""
"However, later attempts to manipulate the cosocket object will fail and "
"return the actual error status message generated by the failed connect "
"operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:662 8e7a66671b2f4d078f6bde90d0ff7498
msgid ""
"This issue is due to limitations in the Nginx event model and only "
"appears to affect Mac OS X."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:666 15e573d176e646b3bb2bf3d36f378c73
msgid "Lua Coroutine Yielding/Resuming"
msgstr "Lua 协程让出/恢复"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:668 daf21095d6604810941525d901e063f1
msgid ""
"Because Lua's `dofile` and `require` builtins are currently implemented "
"as C functions in LuaJIT 2.0/2.1, if the Lua file being loaded by "
"`dofile` or `require` invokes "
"[ngx.location.capture*](#ngxlocationcapture), [ngx.exec](#ngxexec), "
"[ngx.exit](#ngxexit), or other API functions requiring yielding in the "
"*top-level* scope of the Lua file, then the Lua error \"attempt to yield "
"across C-call boundary\" will be raised. To avoid this, put these calls "
"requiring yielding into your own Lua functions in the Lua file instead of"
" the top-level scope of the file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:672 47ce37a4bc834e2b89961f5c28dbc00e
msgid "Lua Variable Scope"
msgstr "Lua 变量作用域"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:674 4ede01ddb2394cd2ab694d731d33f2d1
msgid "Care must be taken when importing modules, and this form should be used:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:681 9bbb5836d1e24f1993bd6522aa669c6b
msgid "instead of the old deprecated form:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:688 20500c574e164c3dafd01532e61e3ef3
msgid ""
"Here is the reason: by design, the global environment has exactly the "
"same lifetime as the Nginx request handler associated with it. Each "
"request handler has its own set of Lua global variables and that is the "
"idea of request isolation. The Lua module is actually loaded by the first"
" Nginx request handler and is cached by the `require()` built-in in the "
"`package.loaded` table for later reference, and the `module()` builtin "
"used by some Lua modules has the side effect of setting a global variable"
" to the loaded module table. But this global variable will be cleared at "
"the end of the request handler,  and every subsequent request handler all"
" has its own (clean) global environment. So one will get Lua exception "
"for accessing the `nil` value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:690 12a285bd9a0942d9867e08bca773123a
msgid ""
"The use of Lua global variables is a generally inadvisable in the ngx_lua"
" context as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:692 6646535573fc484bb34fc21f9e6d3142
msgid ""
"the misuse of Lua globals has detrimental side effects on concurrent "
"requests when such variables should instead be local in scope,"
msgstr "当本应作为局部变量使用时，误用 Lua 全局变量会对并发请求产生有害的副作用，"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:693 94f0922edc5f43e79fbed5be7ce02cce
msgid ""
"Lua global variables require Lua table look-ups in the global environment"
" which is computationally expensive, and"
msgstr "Lua 全局变量需要在全局环境中做表查找，计算开销很大，并且"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:694 3ac20ceb15e44b06bdc95bd2e026698b
msgid ""
"some Lua global variable references may include typing errors which make "
"such difficult to debug."
msgstr "某些 Lua 全局变量引用可能存在拼写错误，使这类问题难以调试。"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:696 4dd83585aca7493393b559936a581cc4
msgid ""
"It is therefore *highly* recommended to always declare such within an "
"appropriate local scope instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:711 e946be5ab3384153b5b267bb87e500a9
msgid ""
"To find all instances of Lua global variables in your Lua code, run the "
"[lua-releng tool](https://github.com/openresty/nginx-devel-"
"utils/blob/master/lua-releng) across all `.lua` source files:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:719 9abefe1be0494e86bd4247a252e6dd9c
msgid ""
"The output says that the line 1489 of file `lib/foo/bar.lua` writes to a "
"global variable named `contains`, the line 1506 reads from the global "
"variable `setvar`, and line 1545 reads the global `varexpand`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:721 4054169ae89448b5991b18826f3a6ecf
msgid ""
"This tool will guarantee that local variables in the Lua module functions"
" are all declared with the `local` keyword, otherwise a runtime exception"
" will be thrown. It prevents undesirable race conditions while accessing "
"such variables. See [Data Sharing within an Nginx Worker](#data-sharing-"
"within-an-nginx-worker) for the reasons behind this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:725 736484b61639462eb559451f445dcf92
msgid "Locations Configured by Subrequest Directives of Other Modules"
msgstr "由其他模块子请求指令配置的 location"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:727 334952a8cf554632a4a8f576f57c6cd5
msgid ""
"The [ngx.location.capture](#ngxlocationcapture) and "
"[ngx.location.capture_multi](#ngxlocationcapture_multi) directives cannot"
" capture locations that include the "
"[add_before_body](http://nginx.org/en/docs/http/ngx_http_addition_module.html#add_before_body),"
" "
"[add_after_body](http://nginx.org/en/docs/http/ngx_http_addition_module.html#add_after_body),"
" "
"[auth_request](https://nginx.org/en/docs/http/ngx_http_auth_request_module.html#auth_request),"
" [echo_location](http://github.com/openresty/echo-nginx-"
"module#echo_location), [echo_location_async](http://github.com/openresty"
"/echo-nginx-module#echo_location_async), "
"[echo_subrequest](http://github.com/openresty/echo-nginx-"
"module#echo_subrequest), or "
"[echo_subrequest_async](http://github.com/openresty/echo-nginx-"
"module#echo_subrequest_async) directives."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:749 922647acdf2544a99605ca6630cbad44
msgid "will not work as expected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:753 a877b54e5e6c4ea09ad470acc56260b4
msgid "Cosockets Not Available Everywhere"
msgstr "并非处处可用 cosocket"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:755 9353f25d3f5743ff84de040da86d6001
msgid ""
"Due to internal limitations in the Nginx core, the cosocket API is "
"disabled in the following contexts: [set_by_lua*](#set_by_lua), "
"[log_by_lua*](#log_by_lua), "
"[header_filter_by_lua*](#header_filter_by_lua), and "
"[body_filter_by_lua](#body_filter_by_lua)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:757 2ce3b15e4cd448ac8ecfd7ed3944dcc7
msgid ""
"The cosockets are currently also disabled in the "
"[init_by_lua*](#init_by_lua) and "
"[init_worker_by_lua*](#init_worker_by_lua) directive contexts but we may "
"add support for these contexts in the future because there is no "
"limitation in the Nginx core (or the limitation might be worked around)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:759 5ddcf4a8a4084482a4089a5743a3d4a0
msgid ""
"There exists a workaround, however, when the original context does *not* "
"need to wait for the cosocket results. That is, creating a zero-delay "
"timer via the [ngx.timer.at](#ngxtimerat) API and do the cosocket results"
" in the timer handler, which runs asynchronously as to the original "
"context creating the timer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:763 5fc2bb4e44574cae9628618634505487
msgid "Special Escaping Sequences"
msgstr "特殊转义序列"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:765 f4732d9908034e9688f4f7b87d194b1c
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**NOTE** Following the `v0.9.17` release, this pitfall can be avoided by "
"using the `*_by_lua_block {}` configuration directives."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:767 a9e26288a2e94c97ace15e7378c0b584
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"PCRE sequences such as `\\d`, `\\s`, or `\\w`, require special attention "
"because in string literals, the backslash character, `\\`, is stripped "
"out by both the Lua language parser and by the Nginx config file parser "
"before processing if not within a `*_by_lua_block {}` directive. So the "
"following snippet will not work as expected:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:782 2037bc440fe84552936a112a756007be
msgid "To avoid this, *double* escape the backslash:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:797 bb154e27edc6468698e3e79308738761
msgid ""
"Here, `\\\\\\\\d+` is stripped down to `\\\\d+` by the Nginx config file "
"parser and this is further stripped down to `\\d+` by the Lua language "
"parser before running."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:799 9902a061ad554956915b17b1307d9727
msgid ""
"Alternatively, the regex pattern can be presented as a long-bracketed Lua"
" string literal by encasing it in \"long brackets\", `[[...]]`, in which "
"case backslashes have to only be escaped once for the Nginx config file "
"parser."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:814 9f51c6914ffb4c37ad19049754a1e2c0
msgid ""
"Here, `[[\\\\d+]]` is stripped down to `[[\\d+]]` by the Nginx config "
"file parser and this is processed correctly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:816 9fd9a661bee04b72a36c0e711ab56c2a
msgid ""
"Note that a longer from of the long bracket, `[=[...]=]`, may be required"
" if the regex pattern contains `[...]` sequences. The `[=[...]=]` form "
"may be used as the default form if desired."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:832 ddc852f49b8b46e6877aee0eb0cb2a91
msgid ""
"An alternative approach to escaping PCRE sequences is to ensure that Lua "
"code is placed in external script files and executed using the various "
"`*_by_lua_file` directives. With this approach, the backslashes are only "
"stripped by the Lua language parser and therefore only need to be escaped"
" once each."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:844 03eb987caff6412d97be528d19f6a82f
msgid ""
"Within external script files, PCRE sequences presented as long-bracketed "
"Lua string literals do not require modification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:855 f69b73995255494a9c3a4ae4f3655926
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"As noted earlier, PCRE sequences presented within `*_by_lua_block {}` "
"directives (available following the `v0.9.17` release) do not require "
"modification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:870 69c5a8f1255e4db084cf57482c94cc20
msgid ""
"**NOTE** You are recommended to use `by_lua_file` when the Lua code is "
"very long."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:874 0ecb614935504ac78e2e44b38d4d9c13
msgid "Mixing with SSI Not Supported"
msgstr "不支持与 SSI 混用"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:876 5e8f2aa217bd499b94a9704263d9b68d
msgid ""
"Mixing SSI with ngx_lua in the same Nginx request is not supported at "
"all. Just use ngx_lua exclusively. Everything you can do with SSI can be "
"done atop ngx_lua anyway and it can be more efficient when using ngx_lua."
