#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:996 b9462da7280e484ab679cceea76567ec
msgid ""
"The cosocket queue regression in `t/196-socket-keepalive-queue.t` checks "
"handoff, cancellation, and timeout recovery in the rewrite, access, and "
"content phases. Its stress case uses a fixed random seed and runs five "
"rounds for each pool size from one to three. Increase "
"`TEST_NGINX_SOCKET_POOL_ROUNDS` for a longer run in one worker:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1004 1914e33986c84ddeabfde91bb53e8f6d
msgid ""
"Each round waits for all surviving operations, forces garbage collection,"
" and checks that the pool admits exactly its configured number of "
"connections. The test also supports the HTTP/2, HTTP/3, and Valgrind "
"modes of Test::Nginx; its request and QUIC idle timeouts increase with "
"the round count."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1009 4bb5c1398a794e6ba62631f4334b1bd6
msgid ""
"There are also various testing modes based on mockeagain, valgrind, and "
"etc. Refer to the [Test::Nginx "
"documentation](https://search.cpan.org/perldoc?Test::Nginx) for more "
"details for various advanced testing modes. See also the test reports for"
" the Nginx test cluster running on Amazon EC2: "
"<https://qa.openresty.org>."
msgstr ""

