#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1252 ee8e426384db4d8cbdf8673bcaebc01f
msgid "lua_malloc_trim"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1254 3cfaa36e710e42c388ed2e18ba666e9b
msgid "**syntax:** *lua_malloc_trim &lt;request-count&gt;*"
msgstr "**语法**：*lua_malloc_trim &lt;request-count&gt;*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1256 1a18e6d3b38147bdbb0035313b64cb9f
msgid "**default:** *lua_malloc_trim 1000*"
msgstr "**默认**：*lua_malloc_trim 1000*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1260 f1e72482d5f44ced9f8cd2978563f930
msgid ""
"Asks the underlying `libc` runtime library to release its cached free "
"memory back to the operating system every `N` requests processed by the "
"Nginx core. By default, `N` is 1000. You can configure the request count "
"by using your own numbers. Smaller numbers mean more frequent releases, "
"which may introduce higher CPU time consumption and smaller memory "
"footprint while larger numbers usually lead to less CPU time overhead and"
" relatively larger memory footprint. Just tune the number for your own "
"use cases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1266 a3616c11e31140bb920f7df0dc41c972
msgid ""
"Configuring the argument to `0` essentially turns off the periodical "
"memory trimming altogether."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1273 79a4c1e4d9c542669102a83e8cce6244
msgid ""
"The current implementation uses an Nginx log phase handler to do the "
"request counting. So the appearance of the [log_subrequest "
"on](https://nginx.org/en/docs/http/ngx_http_core_module.html#log_subrequest)"
" directives in `nginx.conf` may make the counting faster when subrequests"
" are involved. By default, only \"main requests\" count."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1277 c4b8690c190748c18d9be37904c5446f
msgid ""
"Note that this directive does *not* affect the memory allocated by "
"LuaJIT's own allocator based on the `mmap` system call."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1280 d692811c2d064cedad2f42ffaf135b18
msgid "This directive was first introduced in the `v0.10.7` release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1284 6305c4dd7d3745e9bc238baefad79735
msgid "lua_code_cache"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1285 490b8a0f750447189dca146e4e370b1f
msgid "**syntax:** *lua_code_cache on | off*"
msgstr "**语法**：*lua_code_cache on | off*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1287 7dababa44ec84bf68e6429b8e559a25b
msgid "**default:** *lua_code_cache on*"
msgstr "**默认**：*lua_code_cache on*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1291 ff7bec8fefd142d5bfbc3b22e0d8c099
msgid ""
"Enables or disables the Lua code cache for Lua code in `*_by_lua_file` "
"directives (like [set_by_lua_file](#set_by_lua_file) and "
"[content_by_lua_file](#content_by_lua_file)) and Lua modules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1294 eeb2a63fc9f241dea26107ef9edafc1a
msgid ""
"When turning off, every request served by ngx_lua will run in a separate "
"Lua VM instance, starting from the `0.9.3` release. So the Lua files "
"referenced in [set_by_lua_file](#set_by_lua_file), "
"[content_by_lua_file](#content_by_lua_file), "
"[access_by_lua_file](#access_by_lua_file), and etc will not be cached and"
" all Lua modules used will be loaded from scratch. With this in place, "
"developers can adopt an edit-and-refresh approach."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1299 8922dcf442a0460082f2f7f6fb68a7e4
msgid ""
"Please note however, that Lua code written inlined within nginx.conf such"
" as those specified by [set_by_lua](#set_by_lua), "
"[content_by_lua](#content_by_lua), [access_by_lua](#access_by_lua), and "
"[rewrite_by_lua](#rewrite_by_lua) will not be updated when you edit the "
"inlined Lua code in your `nginx.conf` file because only the Nginx config "
"file parser can correctly parse the `nginx.conf` file and the only way is"
" to reload the config file by sending a `HUP` signal or just to restart "
"Nginx."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1305 5384b805611142259f7d8949afed6e1b
msgid ""
"Even when the code cache is enabled, Lua files which are loaded by "
"`dofile` or `loadfile` in *_by_lua_file cannot be cached (unless you "
"cache the results yourself). Usually you can either use the "
"[init_by_lua](#init_by_lua) or [init_by_lua_file](#init-by_lua_file) "
"directives to load all such files or just make these Lua files true Lua "
"modules and load them via `require`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1310 9d64805cae8248d997e131c1673565a8
msgid ""
"The ngx_lua module does not support the `stat` mode available with the "
"Apache `mod_lua` module (yet)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1313 719202646cbc4c53aa32d41419f56cf6
msgid ""
"Disabling the Lua code cache is strongly discouraged for production use "
"and should only be used during development as it has a significant "
"negative impact on overall performance. For example, the performance of a"
" \"hello world\" Lua example can drop by an order of magnitude after "
"disabling the Lua code cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1319 67fefabd7e38465b90ee8104790166fc
msgid "lua_thread_cache_max_entries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1321 8536bf28cb67401ca661c081a5c40d16
msgid "**syntax:** *lua_thread_cache_max_entries &lt;num&gt;*"
msgstr "**语法**：*lua_thread_cache_max_entries &lt;num&gt;*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1323 003eb26643404915a3d45dd619bc0eb7
msgid "**default:** *lua_thread_cache_max_entries 1024*"
msgstr "**默认**：*lua_thread_cache_max_entries 1024*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1327 a68c42d526054dc19e23ade4a7c1afb8
msgid ""
"Specifies the maximum number of entries allowed in the worker process "
"level lua thread object cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1329 2b7c08fd13b341e985c60dad87a3a01a
msgid ""
"This cache recycles the lua thread GC objects among all our \"light "
"threads\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1331 c485f910e33b4a529cffcb8c5fc85420
msgid "A zero value of `<num>` disables the cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1333 2e93ae70bc9f4ae0857eff67f71ada2f
msgid ""
"Note that this feature requires OpenResty's LuaJIT with the new C API "
"`lua_resetthread`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1335 1c3046f63b7d4d29b0e88b431df6777d
msgid "This feature was first introduced in version `v0.10.9`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1339 1d567abba5ea46359ec3d0620278daa6
msgid "lua_regex_cache_max_entries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1341 cbd2c5efbf49435bb3e73ef288fdd302
msgid "**syntax:** *lua_regex_cache_max_entries &lt;num&gt;*"
msgstr "**语法**：*lua_regex_cache_max_entries &lt;num&gt;*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1343 7217402f8e074d069ac3152a0469cdf2
msgid "**default:** *lua_regex_cache_max_entries 1024*"
msgstr "**默认**：*lua_regex_cache_max_entries 1024*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1347 5b0ec98dfd764db28b1f86dcd9cba722
msgid ""
"Specifies the maximum number of entries allowed in the worker process "
"level compiled regex cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1349 17bf01da8f794537b3286d673d98e786
msgid ""
"The regular expressions used in [ngx.re.match](#ngxrematch), "
"[ngx.re.gmatch](#ngxregmatch), [ngx.re.sub](#ngxresub), and "
"[ngx.re.gsub](#ngxregsub) will be cached within this cache if the regex "
"option `o` (i.e., compile-once flag) is specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1351 a0b5e5b604344be89befdd9168f625f6
msgid ""
"The default number of entries allowed is 1024 and when this limit is "
"reached, new regular expressions will not be cached (as if the `o` option"
" was not specified) and there will be one, and only one, warning in the "
"`error.log` file:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1357 fa5e701839de45189c042954ac578722
msgid ""
"If you are using the `ngx.re.*` implementation of [lua-resty-"
"core](https://github.com/openresty/lua-resty-core) by loading the "
"`resty.core.regex` module (or just the `resty.core` module), then an LRU "
"cache is used for the regex cache being used here."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1359 15fc9a13171841c88f79c48847633429
msgid ""
"Do not activate the `o` option for regular expressions (and/or `replace` "
"string arguments for [ngx.re.sub](#ngxresub) and "
"[ngx.re.gsub](#ngxregsub)) that are generated *on the fly* and give rise "
"to infinite variations to avoid hitting the specified limit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1363 6d559a2e950f4d71aafebcdea9f2bed2
msgid "lua_regex_match_limit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1365 5d9bcaa923974a52bcc0cc8149b80d41
msgid "**syntax:** *lua_regex_match_limit &lt;num&gt;*"
msgstr "**语法**：*lua_regex_match_limit &lt;num&gt;*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1367 ebae2a0186984ed19cc6c2350c19ddb4
msgid "**default:** *lua_regex_match_limit 0*"
msgstr "**默认**：*lua_regex_match_limit 0*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1371 4120a7d60bb742e093b08fa878083b56
msgid ""
"Specifies the \"match limit\" used by the PCRE library when executing the"
" [ngx.re API](#ngxrematch). To quote the PCRE manpage, \"the limit ... "
"has the effect of limiting the amount of backtracking that can take "
"place.\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1373 ea3e4343319148d2b762d08be099f543
msgid ""
"When the limit is hit, the error string \"pcre_exec() failed: -8\" will "
"be returned by the [ngx.re API](#ngxrematch) functions on the Lua land."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:1375 9c72090b55924b3a98b0e6850627a30e
msgid ""
"When setting the limit to 0, the default \"match limit\" when compiling "
"the PCRE library is used. And this is the default value of this "
"directive."
msgstr ""

