msgstr "**语法**：*ssl_client_hello_by_lua_block { lua-script }*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:2764 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:2867
#: 9fc54ddc79164c2c98264f3d22f1b661 cea914270b56415ba328a41fc1aca092
msgid "**phase:** *right-after-client-hello-message-was-processed*"
msgstr "**阶段**：*right-after-client-hello-message-was-processed*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:2766 92c819994aa443c3ae0044617ac4e098
msgid ""
"This directive runs user Lua code when Nginx is about to post-process the"
" SSL client hello message for the downstream SSL (https) connections."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:2769 24b055bcc74746a7a4dc744b1550bc21
msgid ""
"It is particularly useful for dynamically setting the SSL protocols "
"according to the SNI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:2771 37f86c832dcd4b0bb72404cfa83e1a8e
msgid ""
"It is also useful to do some custom operations according to the per-"
"connection information in the client hello message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:2773 cb96e36d85af47c7afa98f5b0b0a953a
msgid ""
"For example, one can parse custom client hello extension and do the "
"corresponding handling in pure Lua."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:2775 c9b4e4316d904d80916d7a0efe821cd1
msgid ""
"This Lua handler will always run whether the SSL session is resumed (via "
"SSL session IDs or TLS session tickets) or not. While the "
"`ssl_certificate_by_lua*` Lua handler will only runs when initiating a "
"full SSL handshake."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:2778 a7d0006c7d06460eac66d6f61ef48196
msgid ""
"The [ngx.ssl.clienthello](https://github.com/openresty/lua-resty-"
"core/blob/master/lib/ngx/ssl/clienthello.md) Lua modules provided by the "
"[lua-resty-core](https://github.com/openresty/lua-resty-core/#readme) "
"library are particularly useful in this context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:2782 2673832b6c8f46caa437b7f4755e5c9e
msgid ""
"Note that this handler runs in extremely early stage of SSL handshake, "
"before the SSL client hello extensions are parsed. So you can not use "
"some Lua API like `ssl.server_name()` which is dependent on the later "
"stage's processing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:2785 ceb1e842609c4d0db1bd0cfee0bdfc4c
msgid ""
"Also note that only the directive in default server is valid for several "
"virtual servers with the same IP address and port."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:2787 975427d51f834ff1b602998af6fff86d
msgid ""
"Below is a trivial example using the "
"[ngx.ssl.clienthello](https://github.com/openresty/lua-resty-"
"core/blob/master/lib/ngx/ssl/clienthello.md) module at the same time:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:2824 936720f5aa4d434b9e61f1a71b90e9bf
msgid ""
"See more information in the "
"[ngx.ssl.clienthello](https://github.com/openresty/lua-resty-"
"core/blob/master/lib/ngx/ssl/clienthello.md) Lua modules' official "
"documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:2827 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:2937
#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:3187 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:3271
#: 361161b0328146e8933794b67a8b69b1 6456beddc26842629d1a60fdb642c1a2
#: c43759fcc95a4ba6918a59befb3f7424 d36a237407b54e8699636bd58e0e53ce
msgid ""
"Uncaught Lua exceptions in the user Lua code immediately abort the "
"current SSL session, so does the [ngx.exit](#ngxexit) call with an error "
"code like `ngx.ERROR`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:2830 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:3274
