#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:3087 b420ac6217fb44f8b79ef1f927c153b3
msgid ""
"This directive runs Lua code to fetch and save the SSL session (if any) "
"according to the session ID provided by the current SSL handshake request"
" for the downstream. The saved or cached SSL session data can be used for"
" future SSL connections to resume SSL sessions without going through the "
"full SSL handshake process (which is very expensive in terms of CPU "
"time)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:3092 8f31fbc80f4b4e64bc4bf8bec26eca4b
msgid ""
"Lua APIs that may yield, like [ngx.sleep](#ngxsleep) and "
"[cosockets](#ngxsockettcp), are *disabled* in this context. You can "
"still, however, use the [ngx.timer.at](#ngxtimerat) API to create 0-delay"
" timers to save the SSL session data asynchronously to external services "
"(like `redis` or `memcached`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:3096 f476815ed3d34d68b5617cd436f20ae4
msgid ""
"The Lua API for obtaining the current session ID and the associated "
"session state data is provided in the "
"[ngx.ssl.session](https://github.com/openresty/lua-resty-"
