msgstr "**默认**：*lua_check_client_abort off*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:3710 4d28679dd86e409b927f64a0f485f7f2
msgid ""
"This directive controls whether to check for premature client connection "
"abortion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:3712 fec1d120fcc74b14a3b56045f3439d47
msgid ""
"When this directive is on, the ngx_lua module will monitor the premature "
"connection close event on the downstream connections and when there is "
"such an event, it will call the user Lua function callback (registered by"
" [ngx.on_abort](#ngxon_abort)) or just stop and clean up all the Lua "
"\"light threads\" running in the current request's request handler when "
"there is no user callback function registered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:3714 c2ac2079e2b54eacbfb9b3114a230d97
msgid ""
"According to the current implementation, however, if the client closes "
"the connection before the Lua code finishes reading the request body data"
" via [ngx.req.socket](#ngxreqsocket), then ngx_lua will neither stop all "
"the running \"light threads\" nor call the user callback (if "
"[ngx.on_abort](#ngxon_abort) has been called). Instead, the reading "
"operation on [ngx.req.socket](#ngxreqsocket) will just return the error "
"message \"client aborted\" as the second return value (the first return "
"value is surely `nil`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:3716 609b636feb754b8dab650a5f82d0a30c
msgid ""
"When TCP keepalive is disabled, it is relying on the client side to close"
" the socket gracefully (by sending a `FIN` packet or something like "
"that). For (soft) real-time web applications, it is highly recommended to"
" configure the [TCP keepalive](http://tldp.org/HOWTO/TCP-Keepalive-"
"HOWTO/overview.html) support in your system's TCP stack implementation in"
" order to detect \"half-open\" TCP connections in time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:3718 c81b5d25bcf144eb8ce29a175c24765b
msgid ""
"For example, on Linux, you can configure the standard "
"[listen](http://nginx.org/en/docs/http/ngx_http_core_module.html#listen) "
"directive in your `nginx.conf` file like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:3725 7ab096bd18ba4e0ca63ec889f30f4c35
msgid ""
"On FreeBSD, you can only tune the system-wide configuration for TCP "
"keepalive, for example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:3730 0ec26617132243b78a3ffffa66e413db
msgid "This directive was first introduced in the `v0.7.4` release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:3732 320bbb8d3da14a77a04747a6d210404c
msgid "See also [ngx.on_abort](#ngxon_abort)."
msgstr ""

