msgid ""
"Note that only already defined Nginx variables can be written to. For "
"example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4076 1a4a14564e6943dd92f4bb23b239f39c
msgid ""
"That is, Nginx variables cannot be created on-the-fly. Here is a list of "
"pre-defined [Nginx variables](http://nginx.org/en/docs/varindex.html)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4079 000380d3ee454923a50c5ebf3426f336
msgid ""
"Some special Nginx variables like `$args` and `$limit_rate` can be "
"assigned a value, many others are not, like `$query_string`, "
"`$arg_PARAMETER`, and `$http_NAME`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4082 98e955db17634c029e8bf27a76e40af8
msgid ""
"Nginx regex group capturing variables `$1`, `$2`, `$3`, and etc, can be "
"read by this interface as well, by writing `ngx.var[1]`, `ngx.var[2]`, "
"`ngx.var[3]`, and etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4085 749a766106614fbcaf679e3a4a688038
msgid ""
"Setting `ngx.var.Foo` to a `nil` value will unset the `$Foo` Nginx "
"variable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4092 64192c270cc848f5826195de84011d4e
msgid ""
"**CAUTION** When reading from an Nginx variable, Nginx will allocate "
"memory in the per-request memory pool which is freed only at request "
"termination. So when you need to read from an Nginx variable repeatedly "
"in your Lua code, cache the Nginx variable value to your own Lua "
"variable, for example,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4100 f4dd8ec2530b4ff384578afca753ff0e
msgid ""
"to prevent (temporary) memory leaking within the current request's "
"lifetime. Another way of caching the result is to use the "
"[ngx.ctx](#ngxctx) table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4102 b0ad895e042240b6b2d1af1c51f3c3b5
msgid ""
"Undefined Nginx variables are evaluated to `nil` while uninitialized (but"
" defined) Nginx variables are evaluated to an empty Lua string."
msgstr ""

