#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4254 8f2e275e58f34eb9adb27db36837b30b
msgid "Consider the following example,"
msgstr "请看下面的例子，"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4271 2a95280493a948938c3574df13d56327
msgid "Then `GET /test` will yield the output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4278 99ec59b0142146ff96b9eb9b54c6a278
msgid ""
"That is, the `ngx.ctx.foo` entry persists across the rewrite, access, and"
" content phases of a request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4280 e534c02df9d642ff9f366ec597976472
msgid ""
"Every request, including subrequests, has its own copy of the table. For "
"example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4303 52bc4d24ff5a4ab8b23cd033929199d5
msgid "Then `GET /main` will give the output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4313 8dda6d78500441e997adb594d786f6a7
msgid ""
"Here, modification of the `ngx.ctx.blah` entry in the subrequest does not"
" affect the one in the parent request. This is because they have two "
"separate versions of `ngx.ctx.blah`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4315 66150abc5aa34993b975a827cefc5c54
msgid ""
"Internal redirects (triggered by nginx configuration directives like "
"`error_page`, `try_files`, `index`, etc.) will destroy the original "
"request `ngx.ctx` data (if any) and the new request will have an empty "
"`ngx.ctx` table. For instance,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4333 3a318a6c8648499bb81941831b997883
msgid "Then `GET /orig` will give"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4340 3cad8c8b6272422d91bc075cdc9395f9
msgid "rather than the original `\"hello\"` value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4342 061bd0d9cc8d4847bafed17e2a1ebc24
msgid ""
"Because HTTP request is created after SSL handshake, the `ngx.ctx` "
"created in [ssl_certificate_by_lua*](#ssl_certificate_by_lua), "
"[ssl_session_store_by_lua*](#ssl_session_store_by_lua), "
"[ssl_session_fetch_by_lua*](#ssl_session_fetch_by_lua) and "
"[ssl_client_hello_by_lua*](#ssl_client_hello_by_lua) is not available in "
"the following phases like [rewrite_by_lua*](#rewrite_by_lua)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4346 a7ace4dd42b647e983f3f91702dfa92e
msgid ""
"Since `v0.10.18`, the `ngx.ctx` created during a SSL handshake will be "
"inherited by the requests which share the same TCP connection established"
" by the handshake. Note that overwrite values in `ngx.ctx` in the http "
"request phases (like `rewrite_by_lua*`) will only take affect in the "
"current http request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4350 03f7d8181c614c13a0b29d9c7af184ec
msgid ""
"Arbitrary data values, including Lua closures and nested tables, can be "
"inserted into this \"magic\" table. It also allows the registration of "
"custom meta methods."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4352 82b2fd7f6b4f4b089dfc22ef46265ff7
msgid "Overriding `ngx.ctx` with a new Lua table is also supported, for example,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4359 2ff083adc0f74ef784d197d601c65703
msgid ""
"When being used in the context of "
"[init_worker_by_lua*](#init_worker_by_lua), this table just has the same "
"lifetime of the current Lua handler."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4361 4b10e2c8aa8c4dffae4664b602aec3ca
msgid ""
"The `ngx.ctx` lookup requires relatively expensive metamethod calls and "
"it is much slower than explicitly passing per-request data along by your "
"own function arguments. So do not abuse this API for saving your own "
"function arguments because it usually has quite some performance impact."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4363 3049d1322f9a48d093f3b2993ae28bcc
msgid ""
"Because of the metamethod magic, never \"local\" the `ngx.ctx` table "
"outside your Lua function scope on the Lua module level due to [worker-"
"level data sharing](#data-sharing-within-an-nginx-worker). For example, "
"the following is bad:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4382 c2bb0b6fe57d441e9d4f109847ffe275
