#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4406 435225721189422c8ffb31734bf0dd11
msgid ""
"Issues a synchronous but still non-blocking *Nginx Subrequest* using "
"`uri`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4408 2a03c4998f6c4d5880348989952488d9
msgid ""
"Nginx's subrequests provide a powerful way to make non-blocking internal "
"requests to other locations configured with disk file directory or *any* "
"other Nginx C modules like `ngx_proxy`, `ngx_fastcgi`, `ngx_memc`, "
"`ngx_postgres`, `ngx_drizzle`, and even ngx_lua itself and etc etc etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4411 c19d0a1211904c0eaaf807572522b0de
msgid ""
"Also note that subrequests just mimic the HTTP interface but there is "
"*no* extra HTTP/TCP traffic *nor* IPC involved. Everything works "
"internally, efficiently, on the C level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4413 70787f0ce780436b9ff3bad428ff2f67
msgid ""
"Subrequests are completely different from HTTP 301/302 redirection (via "
"[ngx.redirect](#ngxredirect)) and internal redirection (via "
"[ngx.exec](#ngxexec))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4415 4eb8bb248eab4b52a9d5bf4c513d5095
msgid ""
"You should always read the request body (by either calling "
"[ngx.req.read_body](#ngxreqread_body) or configuring "
"[lua_need_request_body](#lua_need_request_body) on) before initiating a "
"subrequest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4417 9f853b94451648f0bf43588f20f32b35
msgid ""
"This API function (as well as "
"[ngx.location.capture_multi](#ngxlocationcapture_multi)) always buffers "
"the whole response body of the subrequest in memory. Thus, you should use"
" [cosockets](#ngxsockettcp) and streaming processing instead if you have "
"to handle large subrequest responses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4420 3d416c14905e4b44aa03f8c17b9c91d7
msgid "Here is a basic example:"
msgstr "这里是一个基本示例："

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4427 206f8a3b92f44b98a14e0cb13737602e
msgid ""
"Returns a Lua table with 4 slots: `res.status`, `res.header`, `res.body`,"
" and `res.truncated`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4429 eb9cce9f6f5549d5bc9a60654674bbf6
msgid "`res.status` holds the response status code for the subrequest response."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4431 2e71aa0a28fe413cbffa12037469c399
msgid ""
"`res.header` holds all the response headers of the subrequest and it is a"
" normal Lua table. For multi-value response headers, the value is a Lua "
"(array) table that holds all the values in the order that they appear. "
"For instance, if the subrequest response headers contain the following "
"lines:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4444 09ad28b2963c455288f16cd7f8d00ac5
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Then `res.header[\"Set-Cookie\"]` will be evaluated to the table value "
"`{\"a=3\", \"foo=bar\", \"baz=blah\"}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4447 cd1fce9675db423ba214650d78dad05a
msgid ""
"`res.body` holds the subrequest's response body data, which might be "
"truncated. You always need to check the `res.truncated` boolean flag to "
"see if `res.body` contains truncated data. The data truncation here can "
"only be caused by those unrecoverable errors in your subrequests like the"
" cases that the remote end aborts the connection prematurely in the "
"middle of the response body data stream or a read timeout happens when "
"your subrequest is receiving the response body data from the remote."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4449 02c6cbdc05f44b17979ca131ec5d97b9
msgid "URI query strings can be concatenated to URI itself, for instance,"
msgstr "查询字符串可以拼接到 URI 本身之后，例如，"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4456 a7da067a30e0422389c79f1b3d08db4d
msgid ""
"Named locations like `@foo` are not allowed due to a limitation in the "
"Nginx core. Use normal locations combined with the `internal` directive "
"to prepare internal-only locations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4460 cb5382b7dd384045a442449c1f8d043f
msgid ""
"An optional option table can be fed as the second argument, which "
"supports the options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4463 2e47de3709c94b67b94e56bf701d8207
msgid ""
"`method`   specify the subrequest's request method, which only accepts "
"constants like `ngx.HTTP_POST`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4465 0e05f86891574f5bbce24c201b1a039b
msgid "`body`   specify the subrequest's request body (string value only)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4467 6de720b376b7404b8e7aa64fbb4c03d9
msgid ""
"`args`   specify the subrequest's URI query arguments (both string value "
"and Lua tables are accepted)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4469 19034f9fca204abf95cbbab8faa46670
msgid ""
"`headers`   specify the subrequest's request headers (Lua table only). "
"this headers will override the original headers of the subrequest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4471 f65ae1ba8c444418800cdcb06c7bb8b6
msgid ""
"`ctx`   specify a Lua table to be the [ngx.ctx](#ngxctx) table for the "
"subrequest. It can be the current request's [ngx.ctx](#ngxctx) table, "
"which effectively makes the parent and its subrequest to share exactly "
"the same context table. This option was first introduced in the "
"`v0.3.1rc25` release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4473 21789f086dfb45a49fdcc96a5fff3e53
msgid ""
"`vars`   take a Lua table which holds the values to set the specified "
"Nginx variables in the subrequest as this option's value. This option was"
" first introduced in the `v0.3.1rc31` release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4475 d8fac1f7f68e436f827a0bcd07309728
msgid ""
"`copy_all_vars`   specify whether to copy over all the Nginx variable "
"values of the current request to the subrequest in question. "
"modifications of the Nginx variables in the subrequest will not affect "
"the current (parent) request. This option was first introduced in the "
"`v0.3.1rc31` release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4477 443650306b5f45ad8ae9ae4d91dc46c0
msgid ""
"`share_all_vars`   specify whether to share all the Nginx variables of "
"the subrequest with the current (parent) request. modifications of the "
"Nginx variables in the subrequest will affect the current (parent) "
"request. Enabling this option may lead to hard-to-debug issues due to bad"
" side-effects and is considered bad and harmful. Only enable this option "
"when you completely know what you are doing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:4479 ef04c577594d40198a78803743580734
msgid ""
"`always_forward_body`   when set to true, the current (parent) request's "
"request body will always be forwarded to the subrequest being created if "
"the `body` option is not specified. The request body read by either "
"[ngx.req.read_body()](#ngxreqread_body) or [lua_need_request_body "
"on](#lua_need_request_body) will be directly forwarded to the subrequest "
"without copying the whole request body data when creating the subrequest "
"(no matter the request body data is buffered in memory buffers or "
"temporary files). By default, this option is `false` and when the `body` "
"option is not specified, the request body of the current (parent) request"
" is only forwarded when the subrequest takes the `PUT` or `POST` request "
"method."
msgstr ""

