#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:5541 98977d573d35438e989445802c1d038d
msgid "ngx.req.set_header"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:5543 45b90024dd404b58af0b42fa854cf5c5
msgid "**syntax:** *ngx.req.set_header(header_name, header_value)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*ngx.req.set_header(header_name, header_value)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:5547 dc74617138af4737b9f3f7b80a92de4c
msgid ""
"Set the current request's request header named `header_name` to value "
"`header_value`, overriding any existing ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:5549 f385cff0252a44ed8df32e19c706e368
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The input Lua string `header_name` and `header_value` should already be "
"well-formed with the URI encoding. For security considerations, this "
"method will automatically escape \" \", \"\"\", \"(\", \")\", \",\", "
"\"/\", \":\", \";\", \"?\", \"<\", \"=\", \">\", \"?\", \"@\", \"[\", "
"\"]\", \"\\\", \"{\", \"}\", 0x00-0x1F, 0x7F-0xFF in `header_name` and "
"automatically escape \"0x00-0x08, 0x0A-0x0F, 0x7F in `header_value`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:5554 7d63b98b75ec4c06b8b1a2d215dba5b9
msgid ""
"By default, all the subrequests subsequently initiated by "
"[ngx.location.capture](#ngxlocationcapture) and "
"[ngx.location.capture_multi](#ngxlocationcapture_multi) will inherit the "
"new header."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:5556 9d07f73ec7f0444eb2581e42326aa0ec
msgid ""
"It is not a Lua's equivalent of nginx `proxy_set_header` directive (same "
"is true about [ngx.req.clear_header](#ngxreqclear_header)). "
"`proxy_set_header` only affects the upstream request while "
"`ngx.req.set_header` change the incoming request. Record the http headers"
" in the access log file will show the difference. But you still can use "
"it as an alternative of nginx `proxy_set_header` directive as long as you"
" know the difference."
msgstr ""

