msgid "**syntax:** *ok, err = ngx.print(...)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*ok, err = ngx.print(...)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6045 7858f49e34c1400696e5d05a6494188f
msgid ""
"Emits arguments concatenated to the HTTP client (as response body). If "
"response headers have not been sent, this function will send headers out "
"first and then output body data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6049 607ff344d12c49799cc627e96c8b0af4
msgid ""
"Lua `nil` values will output `\"nil\"` strings and Lua boolean values "
"will output `\"true\"` and `\"false\"` literal strings respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6051 f4e8a12469184355ad8069f40d31d473
msgid ""
"Nested arrays of strings are permitted and the elements in the arrays "
"will be sent one by one:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6063 94e6ace708ee4cc3a60858a8459aab06
msgid "will yield the output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6070 aa1c3a4220044363b136f79f69e4d7a2
msgid "Non-array table arguments will cause a Lua exception to be thrown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6072 2ad8f8127aef41eea53003335991f4a6
msgid "The `ngx.null` constant will yield the `\"null\"` string output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6074 8d3d13cfcd99493aabca29b5dad37c20
msgid ""
"This is an asynchronous call and will return immediately without waiting "
"for all the data to be written into the system send buffer. To run in "
"synchronous mode, call `ngx.flush(true)` after calling `ngx.print`. This "
"can be particularly useful for streaming output. See "
"[ngx.flush](#ngxflush) for more details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6076 6419a239bebe4f3f8de8212741b2846c
msgid ""
"Please note that both `ngx.print` and [ngx.say](#ngxsay) will always "
"invoke the whole Nginx output body filter chain, which is an expensive "
"operation. So be careful when calling either of these two in a tight "
"loop; buffer the data yourself in Lua and save the calls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6080 38844c18d1a049fa8aa945bbe6f7a19e
msgid "ngx.say"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6082 63ac23d0238d4377ae4a501e9f515216
msgid "**syntax:** *ok, err = ngx.say(...)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*ok, err = ngx.say(...)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6086 a08ce4dea21e469c9e24d561f63dcbb9
msgid "Just as [ngx.print](#ngxprint) but also emit a trailing newline."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6090 b6d529fd94424130a341ec24f865dceb
msgid "ngx.log"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6092 8c3dae9451a14de588ed8106736dc0f6
msgid "**syntax:** *ngx.log(log_level, ...)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*ngx.log(log_level, ...)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6096 9367d5e4a7834a3ab810b92e6019989b
msgid "Log arguments concatenated to error.log with the given logging level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6098 b1eb69dec0654fc2b147315b875f42cb
msgid ""
"Lua `nil` arguments are accepted and result in literal `\"nil\"` string "
"while Lua booleans result in literal `\"true\"` or `\"false\"` string "
"outputs. And the `ngx.null` constant will yield the `\"null\"` string "
"output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6100 21e5582ef6b7467c882bd088c57d4a41
msgid ""
"The `log_level` argument can take constants like `ngx.ERR` and "
"`ngx.WARN`. Check out [Nginx log level constants](#nginx-log-level-"
"constants) for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6106 3adf5b81f7cc4479a85561c7ae132a1b
msgid "ngx.flush"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6108 1c8f39bf3abc4ff3aa0628813762cfbe
msgid "**syntax:** *ok, err = ngx.flush(wait?)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*ok, err = ngx.flush(wait?)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6112 92f726dab3064dfb9f1eb06d0a741238
msgid "Flushes response output to the client."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6114 6e4b8725ca4e40469df1866651c18698
msgid ""
"`ngx.flush` accepts an optional boolean `wait` argument (Default: "
"`false`) first introduced in the `v0.3.1rc34` release. When called with "
"the default argument, it issues an asynchronous call (Returns immediately"
" without waiting for output data to be written into the system send "
"buffer). Calling the function with the `wait` argument set to `true` "
"switches to synchronous mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6116 669471f91cf74f749633299bab5f9327
msgid ""
"In synchronous mode, the function will not return until all output data "
"has been written into the system send buffer or until the "
"[send_timeout](http://nginx.org/en/docs/http/ngx_http_core_module.html#send_timeout)"
" setting has expired. Note that using the Lua coroutine mechanism means "
"that this function does not block the Nginx event loop even in the "
"synchronous mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6118 d44db7cdfe1945d384975d7532a73bce
msgid ""
"When `ngx.flush(true)` is called immediately after [ngx.print](#ngxprint)"
" or [ngx.say](#ngxsay), it causes the latter functions to run in "
"synchronous mode. This can be particularly useful for streaming output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6120 122d5a7f2a3d4bfab6452fad9ccfa271
msgid ""
"Note that `ngx.flush` is not functional when in the HTTP 1.0 output "
"buffering mode. See [HTTP 1.0 support](#http-10-support)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6126 1a5b850db1794d33bfbb5716449962bf
