#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6353 35e933695954419e82b5c603f566ffbc
msgid ""
"Decodes a URI encoded query-string into a Lua table. This is the inverse "
"function of [ngx.encode_args](#ngxencode_args)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6355 20777a9585a24b66b3f8ea2364cdcbdc
msgid ""
"The optional `max_args` argument can be used to specify the maximum "
"number of arguments parsed from the `str` argument. By default, a maximum"
" of 100 request arguments are parsed (including those with the same name)"
" and that additional URI arguments are silently discarded to guard "
"against potential denial of service attacks. Since `v0.10.13`, when the "
"limit is exceeded, it will return a second value which is the string "
"`\"truncated\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6366 e5b768cf0150497796864b9fb957c037
msgid "This method was introduced in the `v0.5.0rc29`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6370 8ef1bb5c4e2b4c948d1f42ccde3e45a6
msgid "ngx.encode_base64"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6372 4e52a74860b24efba2a0b69a2b45ee43
msgid "**syntax:** *newstr = ngx.encode_base64(str, no_padding?)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*newstr = ngx.encode_base64(str, no_padding?)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6376 efadabd423b145fb9e42aac1d78dda6c
msgid ""
"Encodes `str` to a base64 digest. For base64url encoding use "
"[`base64.encode_base64url`](https://github.com/openresty/lua-resty-"
"core/blob/master/lib/ngx/base64.md#encode_base64url)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6378 0d2115a472b240dd9d529371bc17ee5b
msgid ""
"Since the `0.9.16` release, an optional boolean-typed `no_padding` "
"argument can be specified to control whether the base64 padding should be"
" appended to the resulting digest (default to `false`, i.e., with padding"
" enabled)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6382 32a581252a6a4810acf83f2c5c473127
msgid "ngx.decode_base64"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6384 9045a6a551fd41b5835c3b97ee07d6f5
msgid "**syntax:** *newstr = ngx.decode_base64(str)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*newstr = ngx.decode_base64(str)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6388 80bb43cdcff04caa84994b9975f0e3fc
msgid ""
"Decodes the `str` argument as a base64 digest to the raw form. For "
"base64url decoding use "
"[`base64.decode_base64url`](https://github.com/openresty/lua-resty-"
"core/blob/master/lib/ngx/base64.md#decode_base64url)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6390 d5de369ce1c04d43851fef01966227eb
msgid ""
"The `str` should be standard 'base64' encoding for RFC 3548 or RFC 4648, "
"and will returns `nil` if is not well formed or any characters not in the"
" base encoding alphabet. Padding may be omitted from the input."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6394 d27762c4fb08475daedcacdbecf60562
msgid "ngx.decode_base64mime"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6395 bddb80f259ce4220b8b984cfacf864ec
msgid "**syntax:** *newstr = ngx.decode_base64mime(str)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*newstr = ngx.decode_base64mime(str)*"

