#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6672 2ecc20bed2874e7bb0c4ede32093bd4b
msgid "ngx.re.match"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6674 2f15cbe31cd94088bcbaa08dbf652c9e
msgid ""
"**syntax:** *captures, err = ngx.re.match(subject, regex, options?, ctx?,"
" res_table?)*"
msgstr ""
"**语法**：*captures, err = ngx.re.match(subject, regex, options?, ctx?, "
"res_table?)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6678 c3ddee3df32d4b568e91bea094eb4dee
msgid ""
"Matches the `subject` string using the Perl compatible regular expression"
" `regex` with the optional `options`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6680 4ad09c0f3df04a4ba59fc27f27804afb
msgid ""
"Only the first occurrence of the match is returned, or `nil` if no match "
"is found. In case of errors, like seeing a bad regular expression or "
"exceeding the PCRE stack limit, `nil` and a string describing the error "
"will be returned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6682 6103db3a566447849d130b56e653e21b
msgid ""
"When a match is found, a Lua table `captures` is returned, where "
"`captures[0]` holds the whole substring being matched, and `captures[1]` "
"holds the first parenthesized sub-pattern's capturing, `captures[2]` the "
"second, and so on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6707 dee6ea6784c640ab80efb0ab8c37d577
msgid ""
"Named captures are also supported since the `v0.7.14` release and are "
"returned in the same Lua table as key-value pairs as the numbered "
"captures."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6719 92dfc3bcc0ec473583a8f26c1dca39c3
msgid ""
"Unmatched subpatterns will have `false` values in their `captures` table "
"fields."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6731 d7554b0a0de64e34bd2ae0b8908e5493
msgid ""
"Specify `options` to control how the match operation will be performed. "
"The following option characters are supported:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6777 552b1024b4be40848e30d6d10ab394a3
msgid "These options can be combined:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6792 acef5a25db8e4ecfbe303ed3ceda880e
msgid ""
"The `o` option is useful for performance tuning, because the regex "
"pattern in question will only be compiled once, cached in the worker-"
"process level, and shared among all requests in the current Nginx worker "
"process. The upper limit of the regex cache can be tuned via the "
"[lua_regex_cache_max_entries](#lua_regex_cache_max_entries) directive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6794 0633e1c613494ac9aa0880d7f5994ac6
msgid ""
"The optional fourth argument, `ctx`, can be a Lua table holding an "
"optional `pos` field. When the `pos` field in the `ctx` table argument is"
" specified, `ngx.re.match` will start matching from that offset (starting"
" from 1). Regardless of the presence of the `pos` field in the `ctx` "
"table, `ngx.re.match` will always set this `pos` field to the position "
"*after* the substring matched by the whole pattern in case of a "
"successful match. When match fails, the `ctx` table will be left intact."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6812 7aa23212dd334a79a9186786ba98c901
msgid ""
"The `ctx` table argument combined with the `a` regex modifier can be used"
" to construct a lexer atop `ngx.re.match`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6814 23a98214932c4291a1abb9f5f47cee60
msgid ""
"Note that, the `options` argument is not optional when the `ctx` argument"
" is specified and that the empty Lua string (`\"\"`) must be used as "
"placeholder for `options` if no meaningful regex options are required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6816 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6956
#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7023 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7061
#: 480f7e19ccfb459aa4128e6badb0d727 573cc629fa9f4dd58d1faadd0c72bf91
#: 8a9ff59f4ad84d87b64d78e126da9ce2 f1443552007c4e30b29d001cf789acdc
msgid ""
"This method requires the PCRE library enabled in Nginx ([Known Issue With"
" Special Escaping Sequences](#special-escaping-sequences))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6818 de8c80851230444083f7810fb1d405ff
msgid ""
"To confirm that PCRE JIT is enabled, activate the Nginx debug log by "
"adding the `--with-debug` option to Nginx or OpenResty's `./configure` "
"script. Then, enable the \"debug\" error log level in `error_log` "
"directive. The following message will be generated if PCRE JIT is "
"enabled:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6824 bcd9bf32c1e54961bf01850065bf87fd
msgid ""
"Starting from the `0.9.4` release, this function also accepts a 5th "
"argument, `res_table`, for letting the caller supply the Lua table used "
"to hold all the capturing results. Starting from `0.9.6`, it is the "
"caller's responsibility to ensure this table is empty. This is very "
"useful for recycling Lua tables and saving GC and table allocation "
"overhead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:6826 eb00272f144840989ef87ca080a32a62
msgid "This feature was introduced in the `v0.2.1rc11` release."
msgstr ""

