#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7191 e76620efe38f4335a14a1475db32d165
msgid "ngx.shared.DICT.get_stale"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7193 d14a951556aa4b5a92d1adc5e471da47
msgid "**syntax:** *value, flags, stale = ngx.shared.DICT:get_stale(key)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*value, flags, stale = ngx.shared.DICT:get_stale(key)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7197 11687f88fbc648cc8368be74bdc42dd7
msgid ""
"Similar to the [get](#ngxshareddictget) method but returns the value even"
" if the key has already expired."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7199 9b23065188e242dba125cd8c87591f68
msgid ""
"Returns a 3rd value, `stale`, indicating whether the key has expired or "
"not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7201 3e4ae143ab0a44b3bd8b3629b6aeb444
msgid ""
"Note that the value of an expired key is not guaranteed to be available "
"so one should never rely on the availability of expired items."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7203 788ef3d3bd054b4d94a622a643db47a5
msgid "This method was first introduced in the `0.8.6` release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7209 8fcf614523f74427bda8e7be50c0084a
msgid "ngx.shared.DICT.set"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7211 6fe1d084fd6c4b718f8cd3c771e89bfe
msgid ""
"**syntax:** *success, err, forcible = ngx.shared.DICT:set(key, value, "
"exptime?, flags?)*"
msgstr ""
"**语法**：*success, err, forcible = ngx.shared.DICT:set(key, value, "
"exptime?, flags?)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7215 020e89226f254004ad11a5a9eb64a310
msgid ""
"Unconditionally sets a key-value pair into the shm-based dictionary "
"[ngx.shared.DICT](#ngxshareddict). Returns three values:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7217 b2f021d1ac5f42d7b439572f5cb1f013
msgid ""
"`success`: boolean value to indicate whether the key-value pair is stored"
" or not."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7218 fb9e74eacba94b019068b743ab059152
msgid "`err`: textual error message, can be `\"no memory\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7219 75fe1c451a0742669242c2f2ae1caaaa
msgid ""
"`forcible`: a boolean value to indicate whether other valid items have "
"been removed forcibly when out of storage in the shared memory zone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7221 655f01fd829d45698e10cd74fe5d0c9b
msgid ""
"The `value` argument inserted can be Lua booleans, numbers, strings, or "
"`nil`. Their value type will also be stored into the dictionary and the "
"same data type can be retrieved later via the [get](#ngxshareddictget) "
"method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7223 f6ab9842b8514a9493d868675bfd2530
msgid ""
"The optional `exptime` argument specifies expiration time (in seconds) "
"for the inserted key-value pair. The time resolution is `0.001` seconds. "
"If the `exptime` takes the value `0` (which is the default), then the "
"item will never expire."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7225 77632d9a303b40918a5057f34438f28b
msgid ""
"The optional `flags` argument specifies a user flags value associated "
"with the entry to be stored. It can also be retrieved later with the "
"value. The user flags is stored as an unsigned 32-bit integer internally."
" Defaults to `0`. The user flags argument was first introduced in the "
"`v0.5.0rc2` release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7227 28c1212de15f4ef8b457c397d7aac027
msgid ""
"When it fails to allocate memory for the current key-value item, then "
"`set` will try removing existing items in the storage according to the "
"Least-Recently Used (LRU) algorithm. Note that, LRU takes priority over "
"expiration time here. If up to tens of existing items have been removed "
"and the storage left is still insufficient (either due to the total "
"capacity limit specified by [lua_shared_dict](#lua_shared_dict) or memory"
" segmentation), then the `err` return value will be `no memory` and "
"`success` will be `false`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7229 ce9f357edf6848b793dfc4c4292f122b
msgid ""
"If the sizes of items in the dictionary are not multiples or even powers "
"of a certain value (like 2), it is easier to encounter `no memory` error "
"because of memory fragmentation. It is recommended to use different "
"dictionaries for different sizes of items."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7231 8727f6d210a04c689fd7fcfe1139ad1c
msgid ""
"When you encounter `no memory` error, you can also evict more least-"
"recently-used items by retrying this method call more times to to make "
"room for the current item."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7233 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7375
#: bb3a3403fb5f460fb62ce3701b4c247e e156ff11e82c4720995af28b54451c7b
msgid ""
"If this method succeeds in storing the current item by forcibly removing "
"other not-yet-expired items in the dictionary via LRU, the `forcible` "
"return value will be `true`. If it stores the item without forcibly "
"removing other valid items, then the return value `forcible` will be "
"`false`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7255 6c7ea28a9afb4a0c8ea102ed17ac91a3
msgid ""
"Please note that while internally the key-value pair is set atomically, "
"the atomicity does not go across the method call boundary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7261 a05e880349f24f149f2de3c7ce20b8a1
msgid "ngx.shared.DICT.safe_set"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7263 2cf5d75cd0d64a32a527cdacb2a72eb3
msgid ""
"**syntax:** *ok, err = ngx.shared.DICT:safe_set(key, value, exptime?, "
"flags?)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*ok, err = ngx.shared.DICT:safe_set(key, value, exptime?, flags?)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7267 87ec97f0278f48aab7d82bb5098cbf64
msgid ""
"Similar to the [set](#ngxshareddictset) method, but never overrides the "
"(least recently used) unexpired items in the store when running out of "
"storage in the shared memory zone. In this case, it will immediately "
"return `nil` and the string \"no memory\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7269 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7299
#: 539a050d479d42f6b8d72843b60dc43e daecec9bcef14097a30d7c7779d6ad07
msgid "This feature was first introduced in the `v0.7.18` release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7275 f5ded46a328b4eb7b9fe5c80993a9e8a
msgid "ngx.shared.DICT.add"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7277 75c1b4a0f2574ad0a655056421ec61e7
msgid ""
"**syntax:** *success, err, forcible = ngx.shared.DICT:add(key, value, "
"exptime?, flags?)*"
msgstr ""
"**语法**：*success, err, forcible = ngx.shared.DICT:add(key, value, "
"exptime?, flags?)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7281 5cc5c4004cc2437d9bb9e772291bb3de
msgid ""
"Just like the [set](#ngxshareddictset) method, but only stores the key-"
"value pair into the dictionary [ngx.shared.DICT](#ngxshareddict) if the "
"key does *not* exist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7283 8c91d964b6a742c688efa7a9a3c7d484
msgid ""
"If the `key` argument already exists in the dictionary (and not expired "
"for sure), the `success` return value will be `false` and the `err` "
"return value will be `\"exists\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7291 24b3be360be0470f985301df5e5032e5
msgid "ngx.shared.DICT.safe_add"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7293 1ee7fa5a766149e192cb371ddcde7d14
msgid ""
"**syntax:** *ok, err = ngx.shared.DICT:safe_add(key, value, exptime?, "
"flags?)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*ok, err = ngx.shared.DICT:safe_add(key, value, exptime?, flags?)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7297 de226d7be4f946849fb28a630aa64fb4
msgid ""
"Similar to the [add](#ngxshareddictadd) method, but never overrides the "
"(least recently used) unexpired items in the store when running out of "
"storage in the shared memory zone. In this case, it will immediately "
"return `nil` and the string \"no memory\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7305 068278f8129b426a922234621b0c2144
msgid "ngx.shared.DICT.replace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7307 ac5ac79136af439cb677c09018b84dbe
msgid ""
"**syntax:** *success, err, forcible = ngx.shared.DICT:replace(key, value,"
" exptime?, flags?)*"
msgstr ""
"**语法**：*success, err, forcible = ngx.shared.DICT:replace(key, value, "
"exptime?, flags?)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7311 1e19a66f95264ef7ba254b47065d47f2
msgid ""
"Just like the [set](#ngxshareddictset) method, but only stores the key-"
"value pair into the dictionary [ngx.shared.DICT](#ngxshareddict) if the "
"key *does* exist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7313 95aeeee155fb4b8194a29432c2c33966
msgid ""
"If the `key` argument does *not* exist in the dictionary (or expired "
"already), the `success` return value will be `false` and the `err` return"
" value will be `\"not found\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7321 84021539304348128937340de0909b4c
msgid "ngx.shared.DICT.delete"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7323 d7c78298d22145b5954d65b5ce1e5f8e
msgid "**syntax:** *ngx.shared.DICT:delete(key)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*ngx.shared.DICT:delete(key)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7327 1a20a74316f54bad8a03cea2654da23a
msgid ""
"Unconditionally removes the key-value pair from the shm-based dictionary "
"[ngx.shared.DICT](#ngxshareddict)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7329 6024acf990ee4f1f87f4a1b04fc3cdb9
msgid "It is equivalent to `ngx.shared.DICT:set(key, nil)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7337 7c853d9aff49498c9b482c0c8a39a37b
msgid "ngx.shared.DICT.incr"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7339 eeb2d36effa141d38e529be9c6e69f56
msgid ""
"**syntax:** *newval, err, forcible? = ngx.shared.DICT:incr(key, value, "
"init?, init_ttl?)*"
msgstr ""
"**语法**：*newval, err, forcible? = ngx.shared.DICT:incr(key, value, init?, "
"init_ttl?)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7343 c367fc9885274257913b4b8efaf9b12f
msgid "**optional requirement:** `resty.core.shdict` or `resty.core`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7345 b35402748b184b43a223e61dc0a09532
msgid ""
"Increments the (numerical) value for `key` in the shm-based dictionary "
"[ngx.shared.DICT](#ngxshareddict) by the step value `value`. Returns the "
"new resulting number if the operation is successfully completed or `nil` "
"and an error message otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7347 a60322b8cba84777a4cac3f575f8652c
msgid ""
"When the key does not exist or has already expired in the shared "
"dictionary,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7349 aaa7247386c6479f900f5b0f6c2c6bfa
msgid ""
"if the `init` argument is not specified or takes the value `nil`, this "
"method will return `nil` and the error string `\"not found\"`, or"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7350 d6806043bc2a47fd9304d3f3d85c4c93
msgid ""
"if the `init` argument takes a number value, this method will create a "
"new `key` with the value `init + value`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7352 d4e306326190477b9a79d9cdbeffcd0c
msgid ""
"Like the [add](#ngxshareddictadd) method, it also overrides the (least "
"recently used) unexpired items in the store when running out of storage "
"in the shared memory zone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7354 b5cd1a17d0d7408fabf41daa87d73470
msgid ""
"The optional `init_ttl` argument specifies expiration time (in seconds) "
"of the value when it is initialized via the `init` argument. The time "
"resolution is `0.001` seconds. If `init_ttl` takes the value `0` (which "
"is the default), then the item will never expire. This argument cannot be"
" provided without providing the `init` argument as well, and has no "
"effect if the value already exists (e.g., if it was previously inserted "
"via [set](#ngxshareddictset) or the likes)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7356 05babdfa1a664322a0ae5f1fbf0bcab6
msgid ""
"**Note:** Usage of the `init_ttl` argument requires the "
"`resty.core.shdict` or `resty.core` modules from the [lua-resty-"
"core](https://github.com/openresty/lua-resty-core) library. Example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7373 a4adcb157cf7463bb77a2897d094fbff
msgid ""
"The `forcible` return value will always be `nil` when the `init` argument"
" is not specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7377 5954819b4832495c98168a12b47e8063
msgid ""
"If the original value is not a valid Lua number in the dictionary, it "
"will return `nil` and `\"not a number\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7379 1a7d18927a5a4f8b803e1c47cf39e49e
msgid ""
"The `value` argument and `init` argument can be any valid Lua numbers, "
"like negative numbers or floating-point numbers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7381 ddb71b48604a478a9f5416c1f0ce56b6
msgid "This method was first introduced in the `v0.3.1rc22` release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7383 d8eabc25b0c0419687b10db14888b45c
msgid "The optional `init` parameter was first added in the `v0.10.6` release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7385 3187460a80af47c0ad8aff8f387d6daa
msgid ""
"The optional `init_ttl` parameter was introduced in the `v0.10.12rc2` "
"release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7391 a90afff478a8499d81ba47a0ce88f262
msgid "ngx.shared.DICT.lpush"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7393 a157cd2263c04568a19e700980361b97
msgid "**syntax:** *length, err = ngx.shared.DICT:lpush(key, value)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*length, err = ngx.shared.DICT:lpush(key, value)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7397 d68ba1552d1a46e08dcf1dbfe9ae9da6
msgid ""
"Inserts the specified (numerical or string) `value` at the head of the "
"list named `key` in the shm-based dictionary "
"[ngx.shared.DICT](#ngxshareddict). Returns the number of elements in the "
"list after the push operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7399 457ed4670bc343fc885818f099ee7df9
msgid ""
"If `key` does not exist, it is created as an empty list before performing"
" the push operation. When the `key` already takes a value that is not a "
"list, it will return `nil` and `\"value not a list\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7401 3cfad8dba164461d903df0cb81699426
msgid ""
"It never overrides the (least recently used) unexpired items in the store"
" when running out of storage in the shared memory zone. In this case, it "
"will immediately return `nil` and the string \"no memory\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7403 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7417
#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7433 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7449
#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7465 03bf364b2aba4e60b0109a54cdd6caf1
#: 4e465eb06255457fa4255f8eaa4fed1a 659387e0a78844e0a14ec21d29304058
#: d2a3193fbb814619847979f33b52c579 f32dfda22ee94cb8a0a799264e9d7d0e
msgid "This feature was first introduced in the `v0.10.6` release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7409 0b83e4a083804e9a8c0fdcb8ebfde246
msgid "ngx.shared.DICT.rpush"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7411 13c5a12fd1894543b3f48641ab23f636
msgid "**syntax:** *length, err = ngx.shared.DICT:rpush(key, value)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*length, err = ngx.shared.DICT:rpush(key, value)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7415 4394f6d891454d7a8b19dc3e9d3154db
msgid ""
"Similar to the [lpush](#ngxshareddictlpush) method, but inserts the "
"specified (numerical or string) `value` at the tail of the list named "
"`key`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7423 7292a7a7ef30433ba314e1c0ffb5a85d
msgid "ngx.shared.DICT.lpop"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7425 7370de5a174748f5b71bb98de17a0868
msgid "**syntax:** *val, err = ngx.shared.DICT:lpop(key)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*val, err = ngx.shared.DICT:lpop(key)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7429 c81054a880d841038df9f6952707e489
msgid ""
"Removes and returns the first element of the list named `key` in the shm-"
"based dictionary [ngx.shared.DICT](#ngxshareddict)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7431 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7447
#: 8c54d48c235841dc8bb44f43c0d24858 a876e4dcc3194db085766e17b8fc669a
msgid ""
"If `key` does not exist, it will return `nil`. When the `key` already "
"takes a value that is not a list, it will return `nil` and `\"value not a"
" list\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7439 d76f216416d747ef85d562e1c8aa7091
msgid "ngx.shared.DICT.rpop"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7441 cb001535abb54b84be0afb90b19cbf10
msgid "**syntax:** *val, err = ngx.shared.DICT:rpop(key)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*val, err = ngx.shared.DICT:rpop(key)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7445 f779c43df1504cf68ddc7f6f66b537d0
msgid ""
"Removes and returns the last element of the list named `key` in the shm-"
"based dictionary [ngx.shared.DICT](#ngxshareddict)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7455 85d77e6105f740929c3234beb6e0d6ab
msgid "ngx.shared.DICT.llen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7457 4102148573df44b48c4a705ecd197dc8
msgid "**syntax:** *len, err = ngx.shared.DICT:llen(key)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*len, err = ngx.shared.DICT:llen(key)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7461 0bf54b26c4424b4a9171292148dc8b81
msgid ""
"Returns the number of elements in the list named `key` in the shm-based "
"dictionary [ngx.shared.DICT](#ngxshareddict)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7463 79ad67ff47114242acf6caee76ec91af
msgid ""
"If key does not exist, it is interpreted as an empty list and 0 is "
"returned. When the `key` already takes a value that is not a list, it "
"will return `nil` and `\"value not a list\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7471 e29d029c974845b984ad2d1483e13f5c
msgid "ngx.shared.DICT.ttl"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7473 4261277d9f264dc8834831b5e5a945fd
msgid "**syntax:** *ttl, err = ngx.shared.DICT:ttl(key)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*ttl, err = ngx.shared.DICT:ttl(key)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7477 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7514
#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7599 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7630
#: 3d287e8cf56d421a973005c23a4e9214 84a7cba80f65442fb2278afcb5085489
#: 851a1fe572474386b013d9f7ec7521d2 d67a7e25b60b4882861b5656ec9392f5
msgid "**requires:** `resty.core.shdict` or `resty.core`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7479 f5b1ec25221246bd9d7ba3d3f64a8204
msgid ""
"Retrieves the remaining TTL (time-to-live in seconds) of a key-value pair"
" in the shm-based dictionary [ngx.shared.DICT](#ngxshareddict). Returns "
"the TTL as a number if the operation is successfully completed or `nil` "
"and an error message otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7481 1139131a825840198cc8297351d7d402
msgid ""
"If the key does not exist (or has already expired), this method will "
"return `nil` and the error string `\"not found\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7483 fb1d58c7ac8d4efebc4d063b90a65edf
msgid ""
"The TTL is originally determined by the `exptime` argument of the "
"[set](#ngxshareddictset), [add](#ngxshareddictadd), "
"[replace](#ngxshareddictreplace) (and the likes) methods. It has a time "
"resolution of `0.001` seconds. A value of `0` means that the item will "
"never expire."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7485 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7522
#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7604 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7646
#: 47b48011b7024983940a76bfac9528da 564c7a60d0f14111984d6968c1befd68
#: 6246ecc1ac4441d89faed29c0232659c 86fb793a97274ce19cc87367838702ac
msgid "Example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7500 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7539
#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7614 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7656
#: 8eb692c474824cbfb47a8561b2698bf2 d77361402530484c8392b156231a78ba
#: d93983884b35465fb20d960bb16cdcc2 f64db6bc34994dab90394719c5e2ef44
msgid "This feature was first introduced in the `v0.10.11` release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7502 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7541
#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7616 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7658
#: 1632f2fd681d49b38312083e3fe1e86a 6ec9b5285663489587a11a7d804da3ce
#: c4c650110f2449dcba6b21f613397e87 ca1a14affdf5482081e5516c1c2576b7
msgid ""
"**Note:** This method requires the `resty.core.shdict` or `resty.core` "
"modules from the [lua-resty-core](https://github.com/openresty/lua-resty-"
"core) library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7508 05ca398dd9374d4dbdb4592a877d468a
msgid "ngx.shared.DICT.expire"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7510 02fad5e5ccf7487dba46c6f1c5b465b7
msgid "**syntax:** *success, err = ngx.shared.DICT:expire(key, exptime)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*success, err = ngx.shared.DICT:expire(key, exptime)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7516 20470b689c274a218ac63e4bb8f10682
msgid ""
"Updates the `exptime` (in second) of a key-value pair in the shm-based "
"dictionary [ngx.shared.DICT](#ngxshareddict). Returns a boolean "
"indicating success if the operation completes or `nil` and an error "
"message otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7518 fee2050a678a4d42b9607fabe64143fd
msgid ""
"If the key does not exist, this method will return `nil` and the error "
"string `\"not found\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7520 a795fb73a0cb45979d37e535c586fdc4
msgid ""
"The `exptime` argument has a resolution of `0.001` seconds. If `exptime` "
"is `0`, then the item will never expire."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7547 93658650db894b2385cc03a2a7dd0980
msgid "ngx.shared.DICT.flush_all"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7549 d9eb2e7b99bc47369002a51e223aa7e6
msgid "**syntax:** *ngx.shared.DICT:flush_all()*"
msgstr "**语法**：*ngx.shared.DICT:flush_all()*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7553 ff734226667547de8910f2c5a1df2169
msgid ""
"Flushes out all the items in the dictionary. This method does not "
"actually free up all the memory blocks in the dictionary but just marks "
"all the existing items as expired."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7555 463cdba13f8f460db5165deb253a2e3c
msgid "This feature was first introduced in the `v0.5.0rc17` release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7557 7f99f9aca6fe4414b2e929d96df10557
msgid ""
"See also [ngx.shared.DICT.flush_expired](#ngxshareddictflush_expired) and"
" [ngx.shared.DICT](#ngxshareddict)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7561 da7dbf069b3c4df2bd5f95c0b1e7e992
msgid "ngx.shared.DICT.flush_expired"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7563 cc88c20f95054c7ab664d6bb13e12a9a
msgid "**syntax:** *flushed = ngx.shared.DICT:flush_expired(max_count?)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*flushed = ngx.shared.DICT:flush_expired(max_count?)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7567 4a9fd4422b0b448b8b4f8ac366da4884
msgid ""
"Flushes out the expired items in the dictionary, up to the maximal number"
" specified by the optional `max_count` argument. When the `max_count` "
"argument is given `0` or not given at all, then it means unlimited. "
"Returns the number of items that have actually been flushed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7569 1badf116dfa1474e84399b544032b52f
msgid ""
"Unlike the [flush_all](#ngxshareddictflush_all) method, this method "
"actually frees up the memory used by the expired items."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7571 8042e5cb11d44837989b12bc5a1811e4
msgid "This feature was first introduced in the `v0.6.3` release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7573 0cbdb7672dc346e9b9f8da039ae68437
msgid ""
"See also [ngx.shared.DICT.flush_all](#ngxshareddictflush_all) and "
"[ngx.shared.DICT](#ngxshareddict)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7577 4754b641259e47d998a98ffb4bc46be4
msgid "ngx.shared.DICT.get_keys"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7579 8142faaa95fe4546a06072613250121f
msgid "**syntax:** *keys = ngx.shared.DICT:get_keys(max_count?)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*keys = ngx.shared.DICT:get_keys(max_count?)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7583 8bfc97842e424e42acf9a5892d0c14a0
msgid "Fetch a list of the keys from the dictionary, up to `<max_count>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7585 3cfe5d2ae3544d4a831b71de4b92b493
msgid ""
"By default, only the first 1024 keys (if any) are returned. When the "
"`<max_count>` argument is given the value `0`, then all the keys will be "
"returned even there is more than 1024 keys in the dictionary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7587 92d2dbdd37974c588cd483e68d1d9076
msgid ""
"**CAUTION** Avoid calling this method on dictionaries with a very large "
"number of keys as it may lock the dictionary for significant amount of "
"time and block Nginx worker processes trying to access the dictionary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7589 ecd726ab77134d3aa17788735aa54270
msgid "This feature was first introduced in the `v0.7.3` release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7593 05fec07b678443fd976e2f1154cbfea9
msgid "ngx.shared.DICT.capacity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7595 615f004a87364845af5f5bf26213aa11
msgid "**syntax:** *capacity_bytes = ngx.shared.DICT:capacity()*"
msgstr "**语法**：*capacity_bytes = ngx.shared.DICT:capacity()*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7601 78ba81f36a864bb1b9a4c4a276ddb97b
msgid ""
"Retrieves the capacity in bytes for the shm-based dictionary "
"[ngx.shared.DICT](#ngxshareddict) declared with the "
"[lua_shared_dict](#lua_shared_dict) directive."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7618 2ca4dc48883a4147b4d545f0cb3b7322
msgid "This feature requires at least Nginx core version `0.7.3`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7624 ee7d483b49a94b63913245885e417849
msgid "ngx.shared.DICT.free_space"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7626 2c9dd79ca3e84aa4a76e9fe4b5e593a1
msgid "**syntax:** *free_page_bytes = ngx.shared.DICT:free_space()*"
msgstr "**语法**：*free_page_bytes = ngx.shared.DICT:free_space()*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7632 09720de88c77400494ae6d6952dc005c
msgid ""
"Retrieves the free page size in bytes for the shm-based dictionary "
"[ngx.shared.DICT](#ngxshareddict)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7634 c910554bde2d44bb9b8e899c0fddb611
msgid ""
"**Note:** The memory for ngx.shared.DICT is allocated via the Nginx slab "
"allocator which has each slot for data size ranges like \\~8, 9\\~16, "
"17\\~32, ..., 1025\\~2048, 2048\\~ bytes. And pages are assigned to a "
"slot if there is no room in already assigned pages for the slot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7638 16f5c08dc2654e50b66c83416818f7bd
msgid ""
"So even if the return value of the `free_space` method is zero, there may"
" be room in already assigned pages, so you may successfully set a new key"
" value pair to the shared dict without getting `true` for `forcible` or "
"non nil `err` from the `ngx.shared.DICT.set`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7642 45bb9802596243ffbeaadbb1bb0f5ddf
msgid ""
"On the other hand, if already assigned pages for a slot are full and a "
"new key value pair is added to the slot and there is no free page, you "
"may get `true` for `forcible` or non nil `err` from the "
"`ngx.shared.DICT.set` method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7660 a4dac9001bbd4136b57a9232b2c01401
msgid "This feature requires at least Nginx core version `1.11.7`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7666 43616eda04b3408fa5b67a9dd46c9481
msgid "ngx.socket.udp"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7668 754314d6a5e7482989c6324771fbfede
msgid "**syntax:** *udpsock = ngx.socket.udp()*"
msgstr "**语法**：*udpsock = ngx.socket.udp()*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7672 f125070ae9ab4a1dbee1b4d641ca38a9
msgid ""
"Creates and returns a UDP or datagram-oriented unix domain socket object "
"(also known as one type of the \"cosocket\" objects). The following "
"methods are supported on this object:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7674 01e3e26c3b9542aabaf0fc88e7c81654
msgid "[bind](#udpsockbind)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7675 4a7510f51fee484cb0a4e580906bc5c4
msgid "[setpeername](#udpsocksetpeername)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7676 f1286fd37d204176a568cc42b805cf5a
msgid "[send](#udpsocksend)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7677 3394ff83b6224f87a07ff7b7c56e2571
msgid "[receive](#udpsockreceive)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7678 ca1efbc83c764d4d8837a9f46113bcb3
msgid "[close](#udpsockclose)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7679 088c80cf50024784a0fda5bcd54d7547
msgid "[settimeout](#udpsocksettimeout)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7681 caadbe079f69430dbe72d53e60c62e59
msgid ""
"It is intended to be compatible with the UDP API of the "
"[LuaSocket](http://w3.impa.br/~diego/software/luasocket/udp.html) library"
" but is 100% nonblocking out of the box."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7683 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7794
#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7829 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7843
#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7857 2bad53826ac046faafa384f4a46660bf
#: 64ed2c0e5ef04a399cf79c96876c0838 6bd260439fe1426ca710697f99725d0c
#: d4cf26265db44d47a112e2fb6068ebe1 da2f1748579a4ca38e8d7c501addbdb8
msgid "This feature was first introduced in the `v0.5.7` release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7685 58387d2f921e48c895a7212cdd0df49c
msgid "See also [ngx.socket.tcp](#ngxsockettcp)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7689 ece193f0aa81420d9861d6a05bc78fdb
msgid "udpsock:bind"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7690 492bcda8353a407b97411f82508c5409
msgid "**syntax:** *ok, err = udpsock:bind(address)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*ok, err = udpsock:bind(address)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7692 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7925
#: 19c97e8dad2346aebd1603140f25b698 a2bb07541b154157b300c2c0e0c9dc55
msgid ""
"**context:** *rewrite_by_lua&#42;, access_by_lua&#42;, "
"content_by_lua&#42;, ngx.timer.&#42;, "
"ssl_certificate_by_lua&#42;,ssl_session_fetch_by_lua&#42;,ssl_client_hello_by_lua&#42;*"
msgstr ""
"**上下文**：*rewrite_by_lua&#42;, access_by_lua&#42;, content_by_lua&#42;, "
"ngx.timer.&#42;, "
"ssl_certificate_by_lua&#42;,ssl_session_fetch_by_lua&#42;,ssl_client_hello_by_lua&#42;*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7694 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7927
#: 5ce3169527c44902b0fbe1af879747cc dcac76eadf8d4064a845062e3396d1e3
msgid ""
"Just like the standard "
"[proxy_bind](http://nginx.org/en/docs/http/ngx_http_proxy_module.html#proxy_bind)"
" directive, this api makes the outgoing connection to a upstream server "
"originate from the specified local IP address."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7696 906a0c8bb8724b86b923831e53bbaf0c
msgid "Only IP addresses can be specified as the `address` argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7698 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7932
#: 09446c8e8f254fb2ac391ec6a3a72c8c a6574246059b461d97a346dfcef0b95e
msgid ""
"Here is an example for connecting to a TCP server from the specified "
"local IP address:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7718 19adf25375924d5b8d218e20b0053d08
msgid "udpsock:setpeername"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7720 742cc09fbd754ddbb9358b18c80f61d4
msgid "**syntax:** *ok, err = udpsock:setpeername(host, port)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*ok, err = udpsock:setpeername(host, port)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7722 3fc78d278f2a449a90d7b65a500054ed
msgid ""
"**syntax:** *ok, err = udpsock:setpeername(\"unix:/path/to/unix-"
"domain.socket\")*"
msgstr ""
"**语法**：*ok, err = udpsock:setpeername(\"unix:/path/to/unix-"
"domain.socket\")*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7726 23c54b66bcff4c2db9b64710b2b977b5
msgid ""
"Attempts to connect a UDP socket object to a remote server or to a "
"datagram unix domain socket file. Because the datagram protocol is "
"actually connection-less, this method does not really establish a "
"\"connection\", but only just set the name of the remote peer for "
"subsequent read/write operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7728 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7970
#: 1ad4f6a11b184e51bd62af3990271fdd 960a83bdbf644b68b1f3fc651295e2a1
msgid ""
"Both IP addresses and domain names can be specified as the `host` "
"argument. In case of domain names, this method will use Nginx core's "
"dynamic resolver to parse the domain name without blocking and it is "
"required to configure the "
"[resolver](http://nginx.org/en/docs/http/ngx_http_core_module.html#resolver)"
" directive in the `nginx.conf` file like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7735 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7977
#: 9bf6da05506748f594fb258ce424f9c0 b47c414e3cc34b5b97f832d38b9ee027
msgid ""
"If the nameserver returns multiple IP addresses for the host name, this "
"method will pick up one randomly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7737 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7979
#: c12588e5f1f745119657325c90a9e8ea f4041f1546db44b08724fc1e59b32032
msgid ""
"In case of error, the method returns `nil` followed by a string "
"describing the error. In case of success, the method returns `1`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7739 5f8dbd949fdf4d3ca8c7cd7e6d51b070
msgid "Here is an example for connecting to a UDP (memcached) server:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7759 1df67b4e8d8e44de9e1df33f8ad727f0
msgid ""
"Since the `v0.7.18` release, connecting to a datagram unix domain socket "
"file is also possible on Linux:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7774 996f8f55d88c40eb81b3bf642254dd68
msgid ""
"assuming the datagram service is listening on the unix domain socket file"
" `/tmp/some-datagram-service.sock` and the client socket will use the "
"\"autobind\" feature on Linux."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7776 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8029
#: 7815ca549a444042b52ff3d82191cc01 f5ede1d463e142269d87d474868702f5
msgid ""
"Calling this method on an already connected socket object will cause the "
"original connection to be closed first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7778 747a45ac464344f899fa61cedb864291
msgid "This method was first introduced in the `v0.5.7` release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7782 77e551b0e84844c7842d2ba39ee5fc26
msgid "udpsock:send"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7784 c1fc8f9448ea4fada76bdce866742200
msgid "**syntax:** *ok, err = udpsock:send(data)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*ok, err = udpsock:send(data)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7788 8b78e5c0ac8344db90642f792f1324e5
msgid "Sends data on the current UDP or datagram unix domain socket object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7790 4c4016ca797d4737aeadbaa2125b61d4
msgid ""
"In case of success, it returns `1`. Otherwise, it returns `nil` and a "
"string describing the error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7792 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8248
#: 37043b0a92c74b219d39d316fee5920b c8e23f69f8c542edbc1b23b95bae34c4
msgid ""
"The input argument `data` can either be a Lua string or a (nested) Lua "
"table holding string fragments. In case of table arguments, this method "
"will copy all the string elements piece by piece to the underlying Nginx "
"socket send buffers, which is usually optimal than doing string "
"concatenation operations on the Lua land."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7798 1b647eb781b6456e8328934bd1cf7608
msgid "udpsock:receive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7800 4414d677a3f54831bf41bd1381c4c144
msgid "**syntax:** *data, err = udpsock:receive(size?)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*data, err = udpsock:receive(size?)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7804 8a65b0c683d94aee9098c708f76f4873
msgid ""
"Receives data from the UDP or datagram unix domain socket object with an "
"optional receive buffer size argument, `size`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7806 f1eb9c6e848a465aa688bfa200c9c120
msgid "This method is a synchronous operation and is 100% nonblocking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7808 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8320
#: afb70e3e419b440d90f1ddf884e5b8bf e30e7e4757cd49a9b0aa69a0c3b31adc
msgid ""
"In case of success, it returns the data received; in case of error, it "
"returns `nil` with a string describing the error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7810 b229d973a9d64d078cbb5e390b929545
msgid ""
"If the `size` argument is specified, then this method will use this size "
"as the receive buffer size. But when this size is greater than `8192`, "
"then `8192` will be used instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7812 55c6bb217b6647de9993537ed27a8650
msgid ""
"If no argument is specified, then the maximal buffer size, `8192` is "
"assumed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7814 acd20ba3e1024c80a941aecfc230213e
msgid ""
"Timeout for the reading operation is controlled by the "
"[lua_socket_read_timeout](#lua_socket_read_timeout) config directive and "
"the [settimeout](#udpsocksettimeout) method. And the latter takes "
"priority. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7827 1163a594f71441c4b18ee8a1e490977d
msgid ""
"It is important here to call the [settimeout](#udpsocksettimeout) method "
"*before* calling this method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7833 25d5d57e104b449bbe2497c922e95180
msgid "udpsock:close"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7835 825e0120349748479f8a164ed5b25c1a
msgid "**syntax:** *ok, err = udpsock:close()*"
msgstr "**语法**：*ok, err = udpsock:close()*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7839 291157e985ff46debf3ef7c9a85e5ecf
msgid ""
"Closes the current UDP or datagram unix domain socket. It returns the `1`"
" in case of success and returns `nil` with a string describing the error "
"otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7841 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8453
#: 46f272ecb3cd46aca00a3b7ae91e27cf 9dca4e49c8e0477faed3a3e93b14f9bb
msgid ""
"Socket objects that have not invoked this method (and associated "
"connections) will be closed when the socket object is released by the Lua"
" GC (Garbage Collector) or the current client HTTP request finishes "
"processing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7847 680849e2658048169d96a1171b248f3a
msgid "udpsock:settimeout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7849 7fd0740f59cd47eba92505f7843cd0fb
msgid "**syntax:** *udpsock:settimeout(time)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*udpsock:settimeout(time)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7853 47a8ac57e8954d73b5e8eb839fd5863c
msgid ""
"Set the timeout value in milliseconds for subsequent socket operations "
"(like [receive](#udpsockreceive))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7855 0fb81ff8ff804ce5bb195e52bb0e9a22
msgid ""
"Settings done by this method takes priority over those config directives,"
" like [lua_socket_read_timeout](#lua_socket_read_timeout)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7861 ac521a61e5ac46289267402a71d61af4
msgid "ngx.socket.stream"
msgstr ""

