#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7897 36bd2a7547a24886b012667797e2b9cb
msgid ""
"It is intended to be compatible with the TCP API of the "
"[LuaSocket](http://w3.impa.br/~diego/software/luasocket/tcp.html) library"
" but is 100% nonblocking out of the box. Also, we introduce some new APIs"
" to provide more functionalities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7899 f5e45b37e7234b3aa07da5663640d88f
msgid ""
"The cosocket object created by this API function has exactly the same "
"lifetime as the Lua handler creating it. So never pass the cosocket "
"object to any other Lua handler (including ngx.timer callback functions) "
"and never share the cosocket object between different Nginx requests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7901 30943b68bde04a09bc70c2c6c201d3c5
msgid ""
"For every cosocket object's underlying connection, if you do not "
"explicitly close it (via [close](#tcpsockclose)) or put it back to the "
"connection pool (via [setkeepalive](#tcpsocksetkeepalive)), then it is "
"automatically closed when one of the following two events happens:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7906 7410dbb06ea848dd84951c0de9d664c5
msgid "the current request handler completes, or"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7907 87f08a0f174548c8bc179bf7c43c86c3
msgid "the Lua cosocket object value gets collected by the Lua GC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7909 dc3b0f2c5aec4725b560f7bb97cbadc4
msgid ""
"Fatal errors in cosocket operations always automatically close the "
"current connection (note that, read timeout error is the only error that "
"is not fatal), and if you call [close](#tcpsockclose) on a closed "
"connection, you will get the \"closed\" error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7914 ffb9b56c7f6e452dabe5f1168e0832de
msgid ""
"Starting from the `0.9.9` release, the cosocket object here is full-"
"duplex, that is, a reader \"light thread\" and a writer \"light thread\" "
"can operate on a single cosocket object simultaneously (both \"light "
"threads\" must belong to the same Lua handler though, see reasons above)."
" But you cannot have two \"light threads\" both reading (or writing or "
"connecting) the same cosocket, otherwise you might get an error like "
"\"socket busy reading\" when calling the methods of the cosocket object."
msgstr ""

