#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7966 6d9469b6c9874207919ea83466a8752c
msgid ""
"Attempts to connect a TCP socket object to a remote server or to a stream"
" unix domain socket file without blocking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7968 d9464d77b6144c8aa0c6a3a6692a7473
msgid ""
"Before actually resolving the host name and connecting to the remote "
"backend, this method will always look up the connection pool for matched "
"idle connections created by previous calls of this method (or the "
"[ngx.socket.connect](#ngxsocketconnect) function)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:7981 c784c053226c4d9c9ad9452d4b0c7fd0
msgid "Here is an example for connecting to a TCP server:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8001 f8cd46a7aa45454cae075a184e3ace89
msgid "Connecting to a Unix Domain Socket file is also possible:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8016 f21800e8fc5c4e4c8cc595643b52171e
msgid ""
"assuming memcached (or something else) is listening on the unix domain "
"socket file `/tmp/memcached.sock`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8018 4a01989c9bee4fdb9a6728a4697b4a6c
msgid ""
"Timeout for the connecting operation is controlled by the "
"[lua_socket_connect_timeout](#lua_socket_connect_timeout) config "
"directive and the [settimeout](#tcpsocksettimeout) method. And the latter"
" takes priority. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8027 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8258
#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8302 2ab3b066c48f426c8d902c3cb6020e0c
#: 3ac6b83a380649d8bc1c79464f0557e8 e5bd8fb108de4c0f9afb6d2ebebb4bb9
msgid ""
"It is important here to call the [settimeout](#tcpsocksettimeout) method "
"*before* calling this method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8031 28696802d9b44a3fb42f3baa5aa824e5
msgid ""
"An optional Lua table can be specified as the last argument to this "
"method to specify various connect options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8033 564028979b5d483db5b49439fb2a8486
msgid ""
"`pool`   specify a custom name for the connection pool being used. If "
"omitted, then the connection pool name will be generated from the string "
"template `\"<host>:<port>\"` or `\"<unix-socket-path>\"`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8036 8853624389804f58aeeb7eb005458fc7
msgid ""
"`pool_size`   specify the size of the connection pool. If omitted and no"
"   `backlog` option was provided, no pool will be created. If omitted   "
"but `backlog` was provided, the pool will be created with a default   "
"size equal to the value of the "
"[lua_socket_pool_size](#lua_socket_pool_size)   directive.   The "
"connection pool holds up to `pool_size` alive connections   ready to be "
"reused by subsequent calls to [connect](#tcpsockconnect), but   note that"
" there is no upper limit to the total number of opened connections   "
"outside of the pool. If you need to restrict the total number of opened"
"   connections, specify the `backlog` option.   When the connection pool "
"would exceed its size limit, the least recently used   (kept-alive) "
"connection already in the pool will be closed to make room for   the "
"current connection.   Note that the cosocket connection pool is per Nginx"
" worker process rather   than per Nginx server instance, so the size "
"limit specified here also applies   to every single Nginx worker process."
" Also note that the size of the connection   pool cannot be changed once "
"it has been created.   This option was first introduced in the `v0.10.14`"
" release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8056 091100ef6f8644f6b692f0d495ae216f
msgid ""
"`backlog`   if specified, this module will limit the total number of "
"opened connections   for this pool. No more connections than `pool_size` "
"can be opened   for this pool at any time. If `pool_size` number of "
"connections are in use,   subsequent connect operations will be queued "
"into a queue equal to this   option's value (the \"backlog\" queue).   If"
" the number of queued connect operations is equal to `backlog`,   "
"subsequent connect operations will fail and return `nil` plus the   error"
" string `\"too many waiting connect operations\"`.   The queued connect "
"operations will be resumed once the number of active   connections "
"becomes less than `pool_size`.   The queued connect operation will abort "
"once they have been queued for more   than `connect_timeout`, controlled "
"by   [settimeouts](#tcpsocksettimeouts), and will return `nil` plus   the"
" error string `\"timeout\"`.   This option was first introduced in the "
"`v0.10.14` release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8073 317fe5d78bfd4cc8a392fa7baca6c750
msgid ""
"The support for the options table argument was first introduced in the "
"`v0.5.7` release."
msgstr ""

