msgid "This method was first introduced in the `v0.10.29` release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8093 30076ac21e444599b54d2742e539e5b3
msgid "tcpsock:setclientcert"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8095 61df2130a0c44c79b3e1fbed2d367fde
msgid "**syntax:** *ok, err = tcpsock:setclientcert(cert, pkey)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*ok, err = tcpsock:setclientcert(cert, pkey)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8099 7e10d6221c0d46cb88f5761ac5e419aa
msgid ""
"Set client certificate chain and corresponding private key to the TCP "
"socket object. The certificate chain and private key provided will be "
"used later by the [tcpsock:sslhandshake](#tcpsocksslhandshake) method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8102 95d416a20eb446a397ab8cd76cc4dddd
msgid ""
"`cert` specify a client certificate chain cdata object that will be used "
"while handshaking with remote server. These objects can be created using "
"[ngx.ssl.parse\\_pem\\_cert](https://github.com/openresty/lua-resty-"
"core/blob/master/lib/ngx/ssl.md#parse_pem_cert) or "
"[ngx.ssl.parse\\_der\\_cert](https://github.com/openresty/lua-resty-"
"core/blob/master/lib/ngx/ssl.md#parse_der_cert) function provided by lua-"
"resty-core. Note that specifying the `cert` option requires corresponding"
" `pkey` be provided too. See below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8106 ca40f8988c8c43fdbc9d503d511ebee5
msgid ""
"`pkey` specify a private key corresponds to the `cert` option above. "
"These objects can be created using "
"[ngx.ssl.parse\\_pem\\_priv\\_key](https://github.com/openresty/lua-"
"resty-core/blob/master/lib/ngx/ssl.md#parse_pem_priv_key) or "
"[ngx.ssl.parse\\_der\\_priv\\_key](https://github.com/openresty/lua-"
"resty-core/blob/master/lib/ngx/ssl.md#parse_der_priv_key) function "
"provided by lua-resty-core."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8110 1e6ba1723060476182d4288db6be56cd
msgid ""
"If both of `cert` and `pkey` are `nil`, this method will clear any "
"existing client certificate and private key that was previously set on "
"the cosocket object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8113 ce10a7ba31e84e8fa5e2bc3d15ebce8a
msgid "This method was first introduced in the `v0.10.22` release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8117 98d48acdce974f7f8caadfaeef98065c
msgid "tcpsock:settrustedstore"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8119 98b81f47835f457c89aa5b1d11d2acfe
msgid "**syntax:** *ok, err = tcpsock:settrustedstore(x509_store)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*ok, err = tcpsock:settrustedstore(x509_store)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8121 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8662
#: 8af83cbd85434a7ea733f49e2b2d6919 cd715186118a4517978d6cd6fdb4f2c4
msgid ""
"**context:** *rewrite_by_lua&#42;, access_by_lua&#42;, "
"content_by_lua&#42;, ngx.timer.&#42;*"
msgstr ""
"**上下文**：*rewrite_by_lua&#42;, access_by_lua&#42;, content_by_lua&#42;, "
"ngx.timer.&#42;*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8123 705dd97b349c48d1a3ff809a049a0714
msgid ""
"Set an X509 trusted certificate store on the TCP socket object. The store"
" will be used by the [tcpsock:sslhandshake](#tcpsocksslhandshake) method "
"to verify the remote server's certificate, in place of the CAs configured"
" by the [lua_ssl_trusted_certificate](#lua_ssl_trusted_certificate) "
"directive. This is useful when the set of trusted CAs is determined at "
"request time, for example when talking to per-tenant upstreams whose CAs "
"are not known at configuration time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8129 f09fd9106a7146a8b0a318e953935aaa
msgid ""
"`x509_store` specifies an `X509_STORE *` cdata object that will be used "
"during the SSL/TLS handshake. Such an object can be built using the "
"[resty.openssl.x509.store](https://github.com/fffonion/lua-resty-openssl)"
" library or directly via raw OpenSSL FFI bindings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8134 0f7c4e62c4994118a3abb15b495f2dae
msgid ""
"If `x509_store` is `nil`, this method will clear any previously set "
"trusted store on the cosocket object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8137 7c21dc05d02d4b5a8ba97a772e61262c
msgid "The TCP connection must already be established before calling this method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8139 0e73545b30184359b66c75f233217093
msgid ""
"The trusted store only takes effect when the next "
"[tcpsock:sslhandshake](#tcpsocksslhandshake) call is made with "
"`ssl_verify` set to `true`; with verification off, the store is ignored. "
"The store is consumed once per handshake and is not retained across "
"handshakes, so callers wishing to apply it to a subsequent handshake on "
"the same cosocket must call this method again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8146 ab8839ed45994aacaf0afce453b7641c
msgid "tcpsock:sslhandshake"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8148 927ed7388a044d78a4de16f7497ce28c
msgid ""
"**syntax:** *session, err = tcpsock:sslhandshake(reused_session?, "
"server_name?, ssl_verify?, send_status_req?)*"
msgstr ""
"**语法**：*session, err = tcpsock:sslhandshake(reused_session?, "
"server_name?, ssl_verify?, send_status_req?)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8152 f672df8bff634395b63840d4d70c5618
msgid "Does SSL/TLS handshake on the currently established connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8154 94d65e2dbeb747389d3f633cd22b7cba
msgid ""
"The optional `reused_session` argument can take a former SSL session "
"userdata returned by a previous `sslhandshake` call for exactly the same "
"target. For short-lived connections, reusing SSL sessions can usually "
"speed up the handshake by one order by magnitude but it is not so useful "
"if the connection pool is enabled. This argument defaults to `nil`. If "
"this argument takes the boolean `false` value, no SSL session userdata "
"would return by this call and only a Lua boolean will be returned as the "
"first return value; otherwise the current SSL session will always be "
"returned as the first argument in case of successes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8164 680a827b1cd34ea48b43c0faa839d025
msgid ""
"The optional `server_name` argument is used to specify the server name "
"for the new TLS extension Server Name Indication (SNI). Use of SNI can "
"make different servers share the same IP address on the server side. "
"Also, when SSL verification is enabled, this `server_name` argument is "
"also used to validate the server name specified in the server certificate"
" sent from the remote."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8171 d889fbe4365a43a8a9498632a6d03009
msgid ""
"The optional `ssl_verify` argument takes a Lua boolean value to control "
"whether to perform SSL verification. When set to `true`, the server "
"certificate will be verified according to the CA certificates specified "
"by the [lua_ssl_trusted_certificate](#lua_ssl_trusted_certificate) "
"directive, or, if [tcpsock:settrustedstore](#tcpsocksettrustedstore) has "
"been called on this cosocket, by the X509 store supplied there (which "
"takes precedence for this handshake). You may also need to adjust the "
"[lua_ssl_verify_depth](#lua_ssl_verify_depth) directive to control how "
"deep we should follow along the certificate chain. Also, when the "
"`ssl_verify` argument is true and the `server_name` argument is also "
"specified, the latter will be used to validate the server name in the "
"server certificate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8184 ea6cbbdf77d54aa9bb0a3e6c308d0c58
msgid ""
"The optional `send_status_req` argument takes a boolean that controls "
"whether to send the OCSP status request in the SSL handshake request "
"(which is for requesting OCSP stapling)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8187 ccc754de58f348899d26667ab61f705f
msgid ""
"For connections that have already done SSL/TLS handshake, this method "
"returns immediately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8190 0f749f22b2864e26b463a64497f76e72
msgid "This method was first introduced in the `v0.9.11` release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8194 36ead4296568426781a678bd8134086c
msgid "tcpsock:getsslpointer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8196 5761f6ad147a492d85783f86f2d5c17c
msgid "**syntax:** *sslpointer, err = tcpsock:getsslpointer()*"
msgstr "**语法**：*sslpointer, err = tcpsock:getsslpointer()*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8200 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8214
#: 291f5d113212455896e27e32fa470dd3 4393b62930d9433ea45a80ddd7b91eb3
msgid ""
"Retrieves the underlying SSL pointer (SSL_CTX structure) of the cosocket "
"connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8202 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8216
#: 6d1251bcec1f4357b6368152683dffad cb6d1158d43747bca199e99a1ae195a1
msgid ""
"This method provides access to the raw OpenSSL SSL pointer, which is "
"useful when third-party modules or FFI code need to perform low-level SSL"
" operations directly on the connection. This enables cross-module "
"operations and advanced SSL manipulations that are not exposed through "
"the standard cosocket API."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8204 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8218
#: 25b01559a1d84767b621165982e75d79 6357c50817b7485f96533be4906519fd
msgid ""
"On success, returns the SSL pointer as a light userdata that can be "
"passed to C functions via FFI. On failure, returns `nil` and a string "
"describing the error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8208 3b58a2a31876417fb322a41fc5442734
msgid "tcpsock:getsslctx"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8210 c71524ce12de4200af83c7fa21da8c55
msgid "**syntax:** *sslctx, err = tcpsock:getsslctx()*"
msgstr "**语法**：*sslctx, err = tcpsock:getsslctx()*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8222 865f95a6d9394dd0a259d869611fb3d8
msgid "tcpsock:getsslsession"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8224 691a360c64c24c6fab1e6cee03ce456e
msgid "**syntax:** *session, err = tcpsock:getsslsession()*"
msgstr "**语法**：*session, err = tcpsock:getsslsession()*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8228 5505624ed61a4bf0930f8e4e36ae92ca
msgid ""
"Retrieves the SSL session object from the cosocket connection for session"
" resumption purposes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8230 74ed9e919a304d4f8a79f2d7cfb8de2b
msgid ""
"While `tcpsock:sslhandshake()` also returns an SSL session, the server "
"may not have sent the session resumption ticket to the client yet at that"
" point, making the session non-reusable. By calling `getsslsession` after"
" the request completes, you can obtain an SSL session that is more likely"
" to be reusable for future connections. This session can then be passed "
"to subsequent `sslhandshake()` calls to enable SSL session resumption, "
"which reduces handshake overhead and improves connection performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8232 b03a6ecc33f148c6a50dc37a0b05bef3
msgid ""
"On success, returns the SSL session as a light userdata. On failure, "
"returns `nil` and a string describing the error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8236 3cb59d73420d4cec8293e4b893e79bb8
msgid "tcpsock:send"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8238 1b9e1ef84f3e4a999e37a0e2a1af2d56
msgid "**syntax:** *bytes, err = tcpsock:send(data)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*bytes, err = tcpsock:send(data)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8242 e3ce97c6508e460ebde9685dea012043
msgid ""
"Sends data without blocking on the current TCP or Unix Domain Socket "
"connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8244 a01808066fc244898d16dd8a85325d7f
msgid ""
"This method is a synchronous operation that will not return until *all* "
"the data has been flushed into the system socket send buffer or an error "
"occurs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8246 92c486104c9c41efaad81565732b77b7
msgid ""
"In case of success, it returns the total number of bytes that have been "
"sent. Otherwise, it returns `nil` and a string describing the error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8250 bf9034d727f54ad79835cb5ef5372a44
msgid ""
"Timeout for the sending operation is controlled by the "
"[lua_socket_send_timeout](#lua_socket_send_timeout) config directive and "
"the [settimeout](#tcpsocksettimeout) method. And the latter takes "
"priority. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8260 2345585e78a842c5a62d5d279994f0ac
msgid ""
"In case of any connection errors, this method always automatically closes"
" the current connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8266 fbdd6c5cf8cc4c2592b012f08e15bed1
msgid "tcpsock:receive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8268 e1a23b7022294c60b5dbc496f230a885
msgid "**syntax:** *data, err, partial = tcpsock:receive(size)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*data, err, partial = tcpsock:receive(size)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8270 fb9d6780d7d8446aa0e8b337f7182039
msgid "**syntax:** *data, err, partial = tcpsock:receive(pattern?)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*data, err, partial = tcpsock:receive(pattern?)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8274 96e8bd0005ee4f8d983e233bf17de772
msgid ""
"Receives data from the connected socket according to the reading pattern "
"or size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8276 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8318
#: 2424b4a2aea7492aaad594f7771360ec b090ddbc60984a5f9c03348a2a3d1083
msgid ""
"This method is a synchronous operation just like the [send](#tcpsocksend)"
" method and is 100% nonblocking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8278 e1a49541d3c04e0383b84bedaa36fc28
msgid ""
"In case of success, it returns the data received; in case of error, it "
"returns `nil` with a string describing the error and the partial data "
"received so far."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8280 14c460abff3a4366b6ffd02121252666
msgid ""
"If a number-like argument is specified (including strings that look like "
"numbers), then it is interpreted as a size. This method will not return "
"until it reads exactly this size of data or an error occurs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8282 6582d1c586e34e0992f1875fbd206d4c
msgid ""
"If a non-number-like string argument is specified, then it is interpreted"
" as a \"pattern\". The following patterns are supported:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8284 1519dca80b2944e3bd37fc6509808153
msgid ""
"`'*a'`: reads from the socket until the connection is closed. No end-of-"
"line translation is performed;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8285 3d8ad4c50add4029bd68325efcdb3fd8
msgid ""
"`'*l'`: reads a line of text from the socket. The line is terminated by a"
" `Line Feed` (LF) character (ASCII 10), optionally preceded by a "
"`Carriage Return` (CR) character (ASCII 13). The CR and LF characters are"
" not included in the returned line. In fact, all CR characters are "
"ignored by the pattern."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8287 84a105b81e9e4d10ac4da7ff406e6ee7
msgid ""
"If no argument is specified, then it is assumed to be the pattern `'*l'`,"
" that is, the line reading pattern."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8289 03b91805b85248d2baec7276e08e8d39
msgid ""
"Timeout for the reading operation is controlled by the "
"[lua_socket_read_timeout](#lua_socket_read_timeout) config directive and "
"the [settimeout](#tcpsocksettimeout) method. And the latter takes "
"priority. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8304 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8437
#: 09b9d606c69445109b46ac63489940b5 b4e68d31d8b743b1b3d7d8e4ff01e742
msgid ""
"Since the `v0.8.8` release, this method no longer automatically closes "
"the current connection when the read timeout error happens. For other "
"connection errors, this method always automatically closes the "
"connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8310 b516aad300754298948ce09a0df13749
msgid "tcpsock:receiveany"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8312 2cbbb1e67b4e48ba9f77ac32f8df4868
msgid "**syntax:** *data, err = tcpsock:receiveany(max)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*data, err = tcpsock:receiveany(max)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8316 a4420db5c7fa4dcc973f445c57a104be
msgid "Returns any data received by the connected socket, at most `max` bytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8322 3d47f06bd2274a0d87f7f5aef0ae653c
msgid ""
"If the received data is more than this size, this method will return with"
" exactly this size of data. The remaining data in the underlying receive "
"buffer could be returned in the next reading operation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8325 47ac02fbbbea45ceb3f0055a92d20e41
msgid ""
"Timeout for the reading operation is controlled by the "
"[lua_socket_read_timeout](#lua_socket_read_timeout) config directive and "
"the [settimeouts](#tcpsocksettimeouts) method. And the latter takes "
"priority. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8338 d9b3a97a2756465083d294070937ed2d
msgid ""
"This method doesn't automatically close the current connection when the "
"read timeout error occurs. For other connection errors, this method "
"always automatically closes the connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8340 db70f369f33f4a05a82419a03b2335fc
msgid "This feature was first introduced in the `v0.10.14` release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8344 77faf0ac7c6349119c88cbc196911441
msgid "tcpsock:receiveuntil"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8346 2f77360bc7bc4f67aa6fb5d0a812d3aa
msgid "**syntax:** *iterator = tcpsock:receiveuntil(pattern, options?)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*iterator = tcpsock:receiveuntil(pattern, options?)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8350 bf43e37c7f134ac4a7ef59d89595ed5d
msgid ""
"This method returns an iterator Lua function that can be called to read "
"the data stream until it sees the specified pattern or an error occurs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8352 303d3f43b05143b980aab68d6ab73ecd
msgid ""
"Here is an example for using this method to read a data stream with the "
"boundary sequence `--abcedhb`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8364 8c3a430956584b8399342839887e41e9
msgid ""
"When called without any argument, the iterator function returns the "
"received data right *before* the specified pattern string in the incoming"
" data stream. So for the example above, if the incoming data stream is "
"`'hello, world! -agentzh\\r\\n--abcedhb blah blah'`, then the string "
"`'hello, world! -agentzh'` will be returned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8366 635cf4e5c06c4bdaac613393eec3df9e
msgid ""
"In case of error, the iterator function will return `nil` along with a "
"string describing the error and the partial data bytes that have been "
"read so far."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8368 eed5592fe1dd4b4989b1edc8465f37b2
msgid ""
"The iterator function can be called multiple times and can be mixed "
"safely with other cosocket method calls or other iterator function calls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8370 9b5a15b659214740ab5a57e7798c9407
msgid ""
"The iterator function behaves differently (i.e., like a real iterator) "
"when it is called with a `size` argument. That is, it will read that "
"`size` of data on each invocation and will return `nil` at the last "
"invocation (either sees the boundary pattern or meets an error). For the "
"last successful invocation of the iterator function, the `err` return "
"value will be `nil` too. The iterator function will be reset after the "
"last successful invocation that returns `nil` data and `nil` error. "
"Consider the following example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8391 8fbc1d9e05fb45e5864819fa766b40da
msgid ""
"Then for the incoming data stream `'hello, world! -agentzh\\r\\n--abcedhb"
" blah blah'`, we shall get the following output from the sample code "
"above:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8403 8d6d2ee3d613469bb24d91241811c00e
msgid ""
"Note that, the actual data returned *might* be a little longer than the "
"size limit specified by the `size` argument when the boundary pattern has"
" ambiguity for streaming parsing. Near the boundary of the data stream, "
"the data string actually returned could also be shorter than the size "
"limit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8405 d7e095d2df284aca9b1da2fe90bec5e0
msgid ""
"Timeout for the iterator function's reading operation is controlled by "
"the [lua_socket_read_timeout](#lua_socket_read_timeout) config directive "
"and the [settimeout](#tcpsocksettimeout) method. And the latter takes "
"priority. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8420 f28ac920738d45318903a043fccdfcbc
msgid ""
"It is important here to call the [settimeout](#tcpsocksettimeout) method "
"*before* calling the iterator function (note that the `receiveuntil` call"
" is irrelevant here)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8422 55ab25a5b09d45a2aeca9ec63f30a77e
msgid ""
"As from the `v0.5.1` release, this method also takes an optional "
"`options` table argument to control the behavior. The following options "
"are supported:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8424 a8675feff49440de9cdcad3d308fe409
msgid "`inclusive`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8426 674e7aaf067149258017b0d5bd7f6bb7
msgid ""
"The `inclusive` takes a boolean value to control whether to include the "
"pattern string in the returned data string. Default to `false`. For "
"example,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8435 94f947479a6c411ea2ab627fec1a90fc
msgid ""
"Then for the input data stream `\"hello world _END_ blah blah blah\"`, "
"then the example above will output `hello world _END_`, including the "
"pattern string `_END_` itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8443 dd374febca3e47aebde865a14b07afc3
msgid "tcpsock:close"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8445 71004883bb3b44c38974e935508d2a2a
msgid "**syntax:** *ok, err = tcpsock:close()*"
msgstr "**语法**：*ok, err = tcpsock:close()*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8449 331a4192d7ee4cd98932e64b68d20032
msgid ""
"Closes the current TCP or stream unix domain socket. It returns the `1` "
"in case of success and returns `nil` with a string describing the error "
"otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8451 01c16b9e3fdc4c9e8a868228b79d0f00
msgid ""
"Note that there is no need to call this method on socket objects that "
"have invoked the [setkeepalive](#tcpsocksetkeepalive) method because the "
"socket object is already closed (and the current connection is saved into"
" the built-in connection pool)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8459 abad8f8430f6481c975b7625a93acc6a
msgid "tcpsock:settimeout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8461 d64dd0807a504198a428b7187dab72f3
msgid "**syntax:** *tcpsock:settimeout(time)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*tcpsock:settimeout(time)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8465 2c4698108b704f61a556853c4715efe2
msgid ""
"Set the timeout value in milliseconds for subsequent socket operations "
"([connect](#tcpsockconnect), [receive](#tcpsockreceive), and iterators "
"returned from [receiveuntil](#tcpsockreceiveuntil))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8467 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8484
#: 34aadfc886254d56a8f9cb86ac6a16e2 aaf8c9c0245345ff820090645aa45422
msgid ""
"Settings done by this method take priority over those specified via "
"config directives (i.e. "
"[lua_socket_connect_timeout](#lua_socket_connect_timeout), "
"[lua_socket_send_timeout](#lua_socket_send_timeout), and "
"[lua_socket_read_timeout](#lua_socket_read_timeout))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8469 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8488
#: 927e3358ea764bd5b0fe38600ab4a3ec aa2256ecf9114bbf9afc0c6a5d6f10a7
msgid ""
"Note that this method does *not* affect the "
"[lua_socket_keepalive_timeout](#lua_socket_keepalive_timeout) setting; "
"the `timeout` argument to the [setkeepalive](#tcpsocksetkeepalive) method"
" should be used for this purpose instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8475 3726a143c5564f9b83acca1be23dc22a
msgid "tcpsock:settimeouts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8477 9025e114210648a28c12b3fe2087f2d1
msgid ""
"**syntax:** *tcpsock:settimeouts(connect_timeout, send_timeout, "
"read_timeout)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*tcpsock:settimeouts(connect_timeout, send_timeout, read_timeout)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8481 fd4e7f5c02444553b89aa3136fe0ad83
msgid ""
"Respectively sets the connect, send, and read timeout thresholds (in "
"milliseconds) for subsequent socket operations "
"([connect](#tcpsockconnect), [send](#tcpsocksend), "
"[receive](#tcpsockreceive), and iterators returned from "
"[receiveuntil](#tcpsockreceiveuntil))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8486 80f3768cb66f4200b996e59d4a2fa7c9
msgid ""
"It is recommended to use [settimeouts](#tcpsocksettimeouts) instead of "
"[settimeout](#tcpsocksettimeout)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8490 04832537a25642b8a651e9e73386f0e7
msgid "This feature was first introduced in the `v0.10.7` release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8494 7d7d4ac82c524f4c86a25cac216c57f1
msgid "tcpsock:setoption"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8496 980b2c1adb984a8587c00eba5b83df46
msgid "**syntax:** *ok, err = tcpsock:setoption(option, value?)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*ok, err = tcpsock:setoption(option, value?)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8500 847b5410e8dd411d826ec0cad5327466
msgid ""
"This function is added for "
"[LuaSocket](http://w3.impa.br/~diego/software/luasocket/tcp.html) API "
"compatibility, its functionality is implemented `v0.10.18`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8504 d1d3c4ea4b364c39bb1d2ade6845791d
msgid ""
"In case of success, it returns `true`. Otherwise, it returns nil and a "
"string describing the error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8506 110afe745e534f639673cc9bd9e34b19
msgid ""
"The `option` is a string with the option name, and the value depends on "
"the option being set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8508 e7c4ed47b5d7489c8550b2f6fa736d7e
msgid "`keepalive`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8510 db7b729bf0554306859ff58b0d48d120
msgid ""
"Setting this option to true enables sending of keep-alive messages on   "
"connection-oriented sockets. Make sure the `connect` function   had been "
"called before, for example,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8521 74cc8b3a0dd344e4988a8596c9b7044a
msgid "`reuseaddr`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8523 ceeb3d287257415488f2f590416728fc
msgid ""
"Enabling this option indicates that the rules used in validating "
"addresses   supplied in a call to bind should allow reuse of local "
"addresses. Make sure   the `connect` function had been called before, for"
" example,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8534 f6fbef1f881840e68173b773d6666433
msgid "`tcp-nodelay`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8536 dd8626ff95514554bf834ca8642560f3
msgid ""
"Setting this option to true disables the Nagle's algorithm for the "
"connection.   Make sure the `connect` function had been called before, "
"for example,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8546 091ab1605479491282861c47b1ea032b
msgid "`sndbuf`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8548 57c085eb5ed54e699500a2a7d9c2957b
msgid ""
"Sets the maximum socket send buffer in bytes. The kernel doubles this "
"value   (to allow space for bookkeeping overhead) when it is set using "
"setsockopt().   Make sure the `connect` function had been called before, "
"for example,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8559 97e89e15ee834fa988b7a5c1ae15f802
msgid "`rcvbuf`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8561 e09882f9537f4065997d0af383524676
msgid ""
"Sets the maximum socket receive buffer in bytes. The kernel doubles this "
"value   (to allow space for bookkeeping overhead) when it is set using "
"setsockopt. Make   sure the `connect` function had been called before, "
"for example,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8573 af17f2cc9b524a6792a4d5e58ddbe9d6
msgid ""
"NOTE: Once the option is set, it will become effective until the "
"connection is closed. If you know the connection is from the connection "
"pool and all the in-pool connections already have called the setoption() "
"method with the desired socket option state, then you can just skip "
"calling setoption() again to avoid the overhead of repeated calls, for "
"example,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8592 56e51aade9c84b40985d46b5620bed21
msgid ""
"These options described above are supported in `v0.10.18`, and more "
"options will be implemented in future."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8596 e065e736f9924f04a19f05b50da2d554
msgid "tcpsock:setkeepalive"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8598 d75183a7cfd6417ca4035bf5a295ca6a
msgid "**syntax:** *ok, err = tcpsock:setkeepalive(timeout?, size?)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*ok, err = tcpsock:setkeepalive(timeout?, size?)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8602 68c71dcbc99c46cf9cc932fb49f4df35
msgid ""
"Puts the current socket's connection immediately into the cosocket built-"
"in connection pool and keep it alive until other "
"[connect](#tcpsockconnect) method calls request it or the associated "
"maximal idle timeout is expired."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8604 484d4108b9de47ef83fbdcc0f9f6d5c0
msgid ""
"The first optional argument, `timeout`, can be used to specify the "
"maximal idle timeout (in milliseconds) for the current connection. If "
"omitted, the default setting in the "
"[lua_socket_keepalive_timeout](#lua_socket_keepalive_timeout) config "
"directive will be used. If the `0` value is given, then the timeout "
"interval is unlimited."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8606 713aa24fd99345348b3386904613a610
msgid ""
"The second optional argument `size` is considered deprecated since the "
"`v0.10.14` release of this module, in favor of the `pool_size` option of "
"the [connect](#tcpsockconnect) method. Since the `v0.10.14` release, this"
" option will only take effect if the call to [connect](#tcpsockconnect) "
"did not already create a connection pool. When this option takes effect "
"(no connection pool was previously created by "
"[connect](#tcpsockconnect)), it will specify the size of the connection "
"pool, and create it. If omitted (and no pool was previously created), the"
" default size is the value of the "
"[lua_socket_pool_size](#lua_socket_pool_size) directive. The connection "
"pool holds up to `size` alive connections ready to be reused by "
"subsequent calls to [connect](#tcpsockconnect), but note that there is no"
" upper limit to the total number of opened connections outside of the "
"pool. When the connection pool would exceed its size limit, the least "
"recently used (kept-alive) connection already in the pool will be closed "
"to make room for the current connection. Note that the cosocket "
"connection pool is per Nginx worker process rather than per Nginx server "
"instance, so the size limit specified here also applies to every single "
"Nginx worker process. Also note that the size of the connection pool "
"cannot be changed once it has been created. If you need to restrict the "
"total number of opened connections, specify both the `pool_size` and "
"`backlog` option in the call to [connect](#tcpsockconnect)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8632 a2556e5faef846b08a521a5d4cc94ec2
msgid ""
"In case of success, this method returns `1`; otherwise, it returns `nil` "
"and a string describing the error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8634 a97e70de1cce4e77a8d6ab37f5fc91b4
msgid ""
"When the system receive buffer for the current connection has unread "
"data, then this method will return the \"connection in dubious state\" "
"error message (as the second return value) because the previous session "
"has unread data left behind for the next session and the connection is "
"not safe to be reused."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8636 66a2e64d47a74f1da16a55c601ef4ac8
msgid ""
"This method also makes the current cosocket object enter the \"closed\" "
"state, so there is no need to manually call the [close](#tcpsockclose) "
"method on it afterwards."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8642 d8b7606113834e83bf0f6de49f609ae7
msgid "tcpsock:getreusedtimes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8644 4e0aee64db4f4b698fa55da249599d1b
msgid "**syntax:** *count, err = tcpsock:getreusedtimes()*"
msgstr "**语法**：*count, err = tcpsock:getreusedtimes()*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8648 df7873ca3b4941d586fc653b70bd8219
msgid ""
"This method returns the (successfully) reused times for the current "
"connection. In case of error, it returns `nil` and a string describing "
"the error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8650 4819317b9dda4debb3726f687745a242
msgid ""
"If the current connection does not come from the built-in connection "
"pool, then this method always returns `0`, that is, the connection has "
"never been reused (yet). If the connection comes from the connection "
"pool, then the return value is always non-zero. So this method can also "
"be used to determine if the current connection comes from the pool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8656 f6c07f814d9747989c1f96e53da4fd17
