#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8727 384e240c6be4441bb428206e1cafe04a
msgid "ngx.thread.spawn"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8729 a6e42e49972f4435b0c059f08cba9db5
msgid "**syntax:** *co = ngx.thread.spawn(func, arg1, arg2, ...)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*co = ngx.thread.spawn(func, arg1, arg2, ...)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8733 ebe0f3d65586471090732be4105252ad
msgid ""
"Spawns a new user \"light thread\" with the Lua function `func` as well "
"as those optional arguments `arg1`, `arg2`, and etc. Returns a Lua thread"
" (or Lua coroutine) object represents this \"light thread\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8735 7253dd3d69804fdbb1fdbe4b2f126e22
msgid ""
"\"Light threads\" are just a special kind of Lua coroutines that are "
"scheduled by the ngx_lua module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8737 7a1dfe50c54d430c99163e182a2e22ce
msgid ""
"Before `ngx.thread.spawn` returns, the `func` will be called with those "
"optional arguments until it returns, aborts with an error, or gets "
"yielded due to I/O operations via the [Nginx API for Lua](#nginx-api-for-"
"lua) (like [tcpsock:receive](#tcpsockreceive))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8739 81b37b58422e4876a756e47f7eb0a51d
msgid ""
"After `ngx.thread.spawn` returns, the newly-created \"light thread\" will"
" keep running asynchronously usually at various I/O events."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8741 1b71d69c3ed6417382fb32fac4d0c738
msgid ""
"All the Lua code chunks running by [rewrite_by_lua](#rewrite_by_lua), "
"[access_by_lua](#access_by_lua), and [content_by_lua](#content_by_lua) "
"are in a boilerplate \"light thread\" created automatically by ngx_lua. "
"Such boilerplate \"light thread\" are also called \"entry threads\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8743 29aab5c908fa4e029ebdbc72d801396c
msgid ""
"By default, the corresponding Nginx handler (e.g., "
"[rewrite_by_lua](#rewrite_by_lua) handler) will not terminate until"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8745 8f51e452335b4b84890aad4a24cdd276
msgid "both the \"entry thread\" and all the user \"light threads\" terminates,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8746 134744195e11407bbc03a1e99fba53ff
msgid ""
"a \"light thread\" (either the \"entry thread\" or a user \"light "
"thread\") aborts by calling [ngx.exit](#ngxexit), [ngx.exec](#ngxexec), "
"[ngx.redirect](#ngxredirect), or [ngx.req.set_uri(uri, "
"true)](#ngxreqset_uri), or"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8747 51574d62452541f09531c735f70b880b
msgid "the \"entry thread\" terminates with a Lua error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8749 4e071d5f38ba413b81422a69f0f8ce5c
msgid ""
"When the user \"light thread\" terminates with a Lua error, however, it "
"will not abort other running \"light threads\" like the \"entry thread\" "
"does."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8751 44275848e0264d22bb232fef6e535006
msgid ""
"Due to the limitation in the Nginx subrequest model, it is not allowed to"
" abort a running Nginx subrequest in general. So it is also prohibited to"
" abort a running \"light thread\" that is pending on one or more Nginx "
"subrequests. You must call [ngx.thread.wait](#ngxthreadwait) to wait for "
"those \"light thread\" to terminate before quitting the \"world\". A "
"notable exception here is that you can abort pending subrequests by "
"calling [ngx.exit](#ngxexit) with and only with the status code "
"`ngx.ERROR` (-1), `408`, `444`, or `499`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8753 8ebfb65e0b1147c08a177ad043549528
msgid ""
"The \"light threads\" are not scheduled in a preemptive way. In other "
"words, no time-slicing is performed automatically. A \"light thread\" "
"will keep running exclusively on the CPU until"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8755 9e70d57d16ea4aeb934426f2697aaa2d
msgid "a (nonblocking) I/O operation cannot be completed in a single run,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8756 280d367e26514f70a32a58ef5ef11d38
msgid ""
"it calls [coroutine.yield](#coroutineyield) to actively give up "
"execution, or"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8757 04433f0e4269438caf3314a49c89a58f
msgid ""
"it is aborted by a Lua error or an invocation of [ngx.exit](#ngxexit), "
"[ngx.exec](#ngxexec), [ngx.redirect](#ngxredirect), or "
"[ngx.req.set_uri(uri, true)](#ngxreqset_uri)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8759 a840c16e6fb7459e92c1c61563abab72
msgid ""
"For the first two cases, the \"light thread\" will usually be resumed "
"later by the ngx_lua scheduler unless a \"stop-the-world\" event happens."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8761 1c790b8bbf1e4fcc96a4db541fc8077e
msgid ""
"User \"light threads\" can create \"light threads\" themselves. And "
"normal user coroutines created by [coroutine.create](#coroutinecreate) "
"can also create \"light threads\". The coroutine (be it a normal Lua "
"coroutine or a \"light thread\") that directly spawns the \"light "
"thread\" is called the \"parent coroutine\" for the \"light thread\" "
"newly spawned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8763 ab29d69af47d4beeaa30a565e67ffc42
msgid ""
"The \"parent coroutine\" can call [ngx.thread.wait](#ngxthreadwait) to "
"wait on the termination of its child \"light thread\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8765 af8e32d0c3c04429b57544f7574e7c24
msgid ""
"You can call coroutine.status() and coroutine.yield() on the \"light "
"thread\" coroutines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8767 37571b9c8f004f54bc3cdf7e6153a74e
msgid "The status of the \"light thread\" coroutine can be \"zombie\" if"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8769 03fd6fdb04ec494a86585dbc5a02bfea
msgid ""
"the current \"light thread\" already terminates (either successfully or "
"with an error),"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8770 418ae8fb04194812b25d4e1d8a33e62f
msgid "its parent coroutine is still alive, and"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8771 be12dd23d63b47f5b96b4292d098b64e
msgid ""
"its parent coroutine is not waiting on it with "
"[ngx.thread.wait](#ngxthreadwait)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8773 b93695ed70244db68e5f0fc1af4cbd7e
msgid ""
"The following example demonstrates the use of coroutine.yield() in the "
"\"light thread\" coroutines to do manual time-slicing:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8805 aca9c8db44ee4c19a8640886a87a2766
msgid "Then it will generate the output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8818 59715a94b41448779145385e3e3ecac7
msgid ""
"\"Light threads\" are mostly useful for making concurrent upstream "
"requests in a single Nginx request handler, much like a generalized "
"version of [ngx.location.capture_multi](#ngxlocationcapture_multi) that "
"can work with all the [Nginx API for Lua](#nginx-api-for-lua). The "
"following example demonstrates parallel requests to MySQL, Memcached, and"
" upstream HTTP services in a single Lua handler, and outputting the "
"results in the order that they actually return (similar to Facebook's "
"BigPipe model):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8861 ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8964
#: 2004e62ddf4f4d5a9bf4bebfb52e0be7 e5b0ce34c2674e64bf35f597a5564404
msgid "This API was first enabled in the `v0.7.0` release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8865 b944ea2d1f324da3b3a4385cfea8a84b
msgid "ngx.thread.wait"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8867 3debaa38c2754c4eb689c74f9763c98f
msgid "**syntax:** *ok, res1, res2, ... = ngx.thread.wait(thread1, thread2, ...)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*ok, res1, res2, ... = ngx.thread.wait(thread1, thread2, ...)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8871 bd6d99c4901f4a04b1deb66c29fe42a7
msgid ""
"Waits on one or more child \"light threads\" and returns the results of "
"the first \"light thread\" that terminates (either successfully or with "
"an error)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8873 534268b6242b4d60ac2bce5a55315c92
msgid ""
"The arguments `thread1`, `thread2`, and etc are the Lua thread objects "
"returned by earlier calls of [ngx.thread.spawn](#ngxthreadspawn)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8875 09e4c5e512b840edb3db58eddb2889d7
msgid ""
"The return values have exactly the same meaning as "
"[coroutine.resume](#coroutineresume), that is, the first value returned "
"is a boolean value indicating whether the \"light thread\" terminates "
"successfully or not, and subsequent values returned are the return values"
" of the user Lua function that was used to spawn the \"light thread\" (in"
" case of success) or the error object (in case of failure)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8877 cbc573c83d5a440caa03bfde5b72b2fc
msgid ""
"Only the direct \"parent coroutine\" can wait on its child \"light "
"thread\", otherwise a Lua exception will be raised."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8879 bc982f5cc12342bd90d4e35e462da463
msgid ""
"The following example demonstrates the use of `ngx.thread.wait` and "
"[ngx.location.capture](#ngxlocationcapture) to emulate "
"[ngx.location.capture_multi](#ngxlocationcapture_multi):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8909 664a4ac7ca1d4073a3e1bc0c0e08fa10
msgid "Here it essentially implements the \"wait all\" model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8911 1452685605004cd285e8f37997b36bef
msgid "And below is an example demonstrating the \"wait any\" model:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8955 7137e6d53fe64d0ea3c04db09734cb90
msgid "And it will generate the following output:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8968 883bf24ec6474ff892f99baba2df2d43
msgid "ngx.thread.kill"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8970 d7e27c41a33b41e18585c8e505a9a410
msgid "**syntax:** *ok, err = ngx.thread.kill(thread)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*ok, err = ngx.thread.kill(thread)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8974 9b7a0cb01acf43f2b700ec0513d41328
msgid ""
"Kills a running \"light thread\" created by "
"[ngx.thread.spawn](#ngxthreadspawn). Returns a true value when successful"
" or `nil` and a string describing the error otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8976 62e620cdd0534b2d9030d7a0a76eb4bd
msgid ""
"According to the current implementation, only the parent coroutine (or "
"\"light thread\") can kill a thread. Also, a running \"light thread\" "
"with pending Nginx subrequests (initiated by "
"[ngx.location.capture](#ngxlocationcapture) for example) cannot be killed"
" due to a limitation in the Nginx core."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8978 5d7c7345347a4796b62405fd7bde54c1
msgid "This API was first enabled in the `v0.9.9` release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8982 8dee0ba8795942fe95b668e457415c12
msgid "ngx.on_abort"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8984 43130727da7a47abba354fc80cd2ce31
msgid "**syntax:** *ok, err = ngx.on_abort(callback)*"
msgstr "**语法**：*ok, err = ngx.on_abort(callback)*"

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8988 8fca8130591a48f6af2438e6f8806dda
msgid ""
"Registers a user Lua function as the callback which gets called "
"automatically when the client closes the (downstream) connection "
"prematurely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8990 c8a3eb725ff94ab1a3e47e8cf76aa710
msgid ""
"Returns `1` if the callback is registered successfully or returns `nil` "
"and a string describing the error otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8992 ab719a0ae9624a35bbf17ed545f0f623
msgid ""
"All the [Nginx API for Lua](#nginx-api-for-lua) can be used in the "
"callback function because the function is run in a special \"light "
"thread\", just as those \"light threads\" created by "
"[ngx.thread.spawn](#ngxthreadspawn)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:8994 c001ff3bf6c14d90a65a2f2054b02c61
msgid ""
"The callback function can decide what to do with the client abortion "
"event all by itself. For example, it can simply ignore the event by doing"
" nothing and the current Lua request handler will continue executing "
"without interruptions. And the callback function can also decide to "
"terminate everything by calling [ngx.exit](#ngxexit), for example,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:9012 c75ba59df963468c9007a457e8277695
msgid ""
"When [lua_check_client_abort](#lua_check_client_abort) is set to `off` "
"(which is the default), then this function call will always return the "
"error message \"lua_check_client_abort is off\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:9014 a43fc2e66a194e02a282080e03666fe6
msgid ""
"According to the current implementation, this function can only be called"
" once in a single request handler; subsequent calls will return the error"
" message \"duplicate call\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:9016 feaf2f760d6240339afc2ce74ac1c038
msgid "This API was first introduced in the `v0.7.4` release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:9018 a62c353b44494a64a4888e6fecbc866e
msgid "See also [lua_check_client_abort](#lua_check_client_abort)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../08-lua-nginx-module.md:9022 e50ff3609d5f48439fb1d3450cea1fde
msgid "ngx.timer.at"
msgstr ""

